/* 段落记忆 · 词层 3 · 子块 d：词头 → {tw:[关系词,关系类型], en, zh} */
window.APP_MERGE_NET(3,{"sub":"d","par":{"religious":{"tw":[["religion",4],["monk",3],["nun",3],["sacred",5],["tradition",6],["secular",1],["worship",6],["scrupulous",5],["superior",3]],"en":"In the old quarter of the city, a religious festival fills the streets every spring. People of the same religion come from far villages, and a monk and two nuns lead the first walk. They say prayers at a small sacred stone that has stood there for centuries. The tradition is older than the buildings around it. A secular neighbour, who never joins the worship, still opens his shop early and gives free tea to the walkers. He is a scrupulous man and counts every cup. 'Their way is not my way,' he says, 'but I like the day.' A superior of the order thanked him with a wooden bowl.","zh":"城里的老街区每到春天就有一场宗教节庆，把街道填得满满的。同一条信仰下的人从很远的村子赶来，一位修士和两位修女走在队伍最前面。他们在一块有几百年历史的小圣石前祈祷。这个传统比周围的房子还要老。隔壁不信教的那位邻居从不参加礼拜，却照样早早开门，给走路的人免费送茶。他是个细致到会数每一个杯子的人。他说，'他们的路不是我的路，可我喜欢这一天。'修会的一位长上用一只木碗谢了他。"},"summary":{"tw":[["compact",0],["outline",3],["paragraph",6],["concise",5],["succinct",0],["sketch",3],["overview",3],["article",6],["update",6]],"en":"My editor asked for a summary of the report by Friday. She wanted something compact, no longer than one page. I began with an outline of the four main points, then wrote a short paragraph for each of them. The result was too long, so I cut it until it was concise. A succinct opening line, I found, saves three lines later on. I added a rough sketch of the map and a small overview of the costs. The article appeared on Sunday with my name under it. My editor sent one update by message: 'Good, but next time start with the numbers.'","zh":"编辑让我周五前交一份报告摘要。她要的是紧凑的东西，不超过一页。我先列了四个要点的提纲，再各写一小段。结果太长，我就一直删到简明为止。我发现，开头一句精炼的话，后面能省掉三行。我又加了一张粗略的地图草图和一小段费用概览。文章周日登出来，下面署着我的名字。编辑只发来一条更新：'不错，不过下次先摆数字。'"},"solve":{"tw":[["solution",4],["clear",0],["answer",3],["settle",2],["problem",6],["solvent",4],["work",0],["break",3],["understand",2],["process",6],["resolve",0]],"en":"In the school lab we had to solve a small problem with a dirty glass tube. The teacher gave us a clear rule: find a good solvent and let it work. Our first answer was wrong, and the glass began to break in the hot water. It took an hour to understand what had gone wrong. We changed the process and let the mixture settle overnight. By morning a simple solution had formed at the bottom. The teacher smiled and said that to resolve a hard question you must stay calm and try again. It was the best lesson of that term.","zh":"在学校实验室里，我们得解决一个小麻烦：一根脏玻璃管。老师给了我们一条明确的规矩：找一种好溶剂，让它起作用。我们头一个答案错了，玻璃在热水里开始裂。我们花了一个小时才明白哪里出了问题。我们换了做法，让混合液静置了一夜。到早上，底部形成了一份简单的溶液。老师笑了，说要想解开一个难题，就得沉住气再试一次。那是那个学期最好的一课。"},"stimulate":{"tw":[["stimulus",4],["cause",0],["bring",3],["affect",2],["stifle",1],["encourage",6],["stimulant",4],["excite",0],["lead",3],["challenge",2],["boost",6]],"en":"A good teacher knows how to stimulate a quiet class. A small challenge, she says, is the best stimulus for a sleepy mind. She will bring a strange object to the room and lead the students to ask about it. Bright colors and a quick game can excite them and boost their attention. A cup of tea acts as a mild stimulant, but it should not become a habit. What she will never do is stifle a wrong answer, because fear can cause a child to hide and can affect how she learns. Her warm words will encourage even the shy ones to speak. In her class, learning feels less like work and more like play.","zh":"一位好老师知道怎么让安静的班级活跃起来。她说，一个小小的挑战，就是叫瞌睡脑袋清醒的最好刺激。她会带一件奇怪的东西进教室，领着学生去问它的问题。鲜亮的颜色和一场快游戏能让他们兴奋，把注意力提起来。一杯茶算是一种温和的兴奋剂，但不该成为习惯。她绝不会做的一件事，是压制一个错的答案，因为害怕会影响孩子学习的方式。她暖暖的话会鼓励连害羞的孩子也开口。在她的课上，学习不像干活，倒更像玩。"},"submit":{"tw":[["submission",4],["present",0],["return",3],["accept",2],["request",6],["submissive",4],["state",0],["test",3],["apply",2],["recommend",6],["subject",3]],"en":"Before the deadline, every student had to submit a short paper to the head of the department. I planned to present my work in person and to state my main idea in one line. The rule was clear: late answers would not be accepted, and the office would return any paper without a name. My friend was more submissive and simply sent hers by post. She had to apply for special leave, and the teacher agreed to recommend it. The written test on the subject came a week later. My submission was short, but it passed. I still keep the letter of request in a drawer.","zh":"截止之前，每个学生都得向系主任交一篇短文。我打算当面做陈述，用一句话说明我的主要观点。规定很清楚：迟交的答案不予受理，没写名字的文章办公室会退回来。我朋友更顺从，干脆邮寄了过去。她得申请特别休假，老师同意作推荐。那门科目的笔试一周后进行。我的提交很短，但通过了。那张申请信我一直留在抽屉里。"},"tender":{"tw":[["tend",4],["offer",0],["page",3],["boat",2],["tough",1],["pound",6],["warm",0],["companion",3],["change",2],["fresh",6],["sore",0]],"en":"On the boat my aunt would tend a small pot of stew all afternoon. She wanted the meat to turn tender, so she cooked it slowly, a pound at a time. The first piece was tough, but the second was soft enough to cut with a spoon. She would offer each of us a warm bowl and a fresh piece of bread. I read a page of my book and watched the water change from grey to green. My old companion on these trips was a sore back, so I sat still and let the sun do the rest. Cooking on a boat is not easy, she said. Yet the meal was one of the best I can remember.","zh":"在船上，我姑妈整个下午都会守着一小锅炖菜。她想让肉炖得软嫩，所以一点一点地慢慢煨，一次一磅。头一块有些硬，第二块却软得能用勺子切开。她会给我们每人端来一碗热菜和一块新鲜面包。我读了一页书，看着水从灰色变成绿色。这几次出门，我那个老毛病——腰酸——一直陪着我，于是我静静坐着，剩下的交给太阳。她说，在船上做饭可不容易。可那顿饭，是我记得的最好吃的几顿之一。"},"significance":{"tw":[["significant",4],["import",0],["sense",3],["message",2],["important",6],["signify",4],["effect",3],["importance",2],["context",6]],"en":"The small clay bowl in the museum has a significance that few visitors notice. In its own context it was not valuable, yet the message it carries is important. To the people who made it, the shape would signify a promise between two families. A guide explained the import of every mark, and the effect on the crowd was clear. One child asked what the bowl meant, and the answer made sense to her at once. A significant number of such bowls were found in one field. Only when you know the story does their importance appear. History, the guide said, is often hidden in plain things.","zh":"博物馆里那只小陶碗，有着很少有人在意的意义。放在它自己的情境里，它并不值钱，可它承载的信息很重要。对于当初做它的人来说，这个形状意味着两家人之间的一个承诺。讲解员解释了每一道痕迹的含义，对人群产生的影响一清二楚。一个孩子问这碗是什么意思，她一听就明白了。同一片地里，曾出土过数量可观的一批这种碗。只有知道了故事，它们的重要性才会显现出来。讲解员说，历史常常就藏在平常的东西里。"},"utility":{"tw":[["utilise",4],["substitute",0],["use",3],["service",2],["grid",6],["utilitarian",4],["function",3],["quality",2],["vehicle",6]],"en":"The old utility company supplies power to a whole valley. Its main function is simple: keep the lights on, whatever the weather. Workers will utilise every dry day to check the poles and the wires of the grid. When a storm breaks one line, they must find a quick substitute for the broken part. A small service van is the only vehicle that can reach the farthest farm. The design of the station is plain and utilitarian, with no extra decoration. Still, the quality of the work is high, and repairs rarely take more than a day. People use the power without ever thinking of the people who keep it running.","zh":"这家老公用事业公司给整个山谷供电。它最主要的功能很简单：不管什么天气，都得让灯亮着。工人们会利用每一个晴天去检查电线杆和电网上的线路。风暴刮断一条线时，他们得赶快给坏掉的部件找个替代件。一辆小小的维修车，是唯一能开到最远那家农场的车。站里的设计朴素而实用，没有多余的装饰。可活儿干得质量很高，抢修很少超过一天。人们用电时，从不会想到那些让电一直供下去的人。"},"reflect":{"tw":[["reflector",4],["shine",0],["study",3],["think",2],["suggest",6],["speculate",0],["wonder",3],["indicate",2],["change",6],["contemplate",0]],"en":"On the cliff the old lighthouse would reflect a bright beam over the dark sea. A metal reflector behind the lamp helped the light shine twice as far. A young keeper began to study how the light moved, and the results would indicate a small fault in the glass. She could only wonder what the ships saw from far away, and she liked to speculate about their long journeys. She would think about the pattern and then change one mirror to test it. To understand light, she said, you must contemplate it for hours. Her notes would suggest a simpler design. By spring the beam was stronger, and the ships came closer to shore.","zh":"悬崖上那座老灯塔，把一道亮光反射到漆黑的海面上。灯后面的一块金属反光板，让光能照出两倍远。一位年轻看守开始研究光是怎么走的，结果显示出玻璃上有一处小毛病。她只能猜想远处的船看到了什么，也爱推测它们漫长的航程。她会琢磨那套样式，然后换掉一面镜子来试。她说，要弄懂光，就得盯着它想上好多个钟头。她的笔记提示出一个更简单的设计。到春天，光柱更强了，船也靠岸更近了。"},"strain":{"tw":[["strenuous",4],["air",0],["tax",3],["shape",2],["virus",6],["form",0],["rice",3],["use",2],["stomach",6],["line",0]],"en":"One hard summer put a great strain on the farmers of the valley. A new virus had attacked the rice, and the loss of a whole field was a heavy tax on every family. The workers were in poor shape after weeks of strenuous work under a hot sky. A scientist came to test the air and to look at the sick plants line by line. She found a second form of the same virus, one that the farmers had never used a spray against. Too much worry began to upset her stomach, she joked. Still, she kept to her plan and stayed until the harvest. The next year, the strain was finally under control.","zh":"有一个难熬的夏天，给山谷里的农民带来了巨大的压力。一种新病毒侵袭了水稻，整片田的损失对每家每户都是沉重的负担。在烈日下苦干了几个星期，工人们的状态很差。一位科学家赶来检测空气，还逐行查看生病的植株。她发现同一种病毒还有第二种类型，是农民从没喷药对付过的。她开玩笑说，操心得太多，胃都开始不舒服了。可她仍然按计划坚持到收割。到了第二年，这种病毒终于被控制住了。"},"technical":{"tw":[["technology",4],["expert",0],["expertise",6],["technique",4],["proficient",0],["work",6],["technicality",4]],"en":"The repair shop takes on the most technical jobs in town. Its owner is an expert in old radios, and his expertise fills a whole wall of notes. He can explain a hard technique in plain words, which is rarer than it sounds. A young helper is now proficient enough to handle most of the work alone. They use simple technology, mostly good tools and patience. Sometimes a single technicality can stop a machine, and finding it takes a whole day. But they never send a job back. A careful hand, the owner says, beats a new machine.","zh":"这家修理铺接的是全城最讲技术的活儿。铺主是修老收音机的专家，他的看家本领写满了整整一面墙的笔记。他能用大白话讲清一门难手艺，这比听上去要少见。一个年轻帮手如今已经熟练到能独立应付大部分活计。他们用的技术很简单，无非是好工具加耐心。有时候一个小技术细节就能让一台机器停摆，找出来要花上一整天。可他们从不把活儿退回去。铺主说，一双细心的手，胜过一台新机器。"},"tragedy":{"tw":[["tragic",4],["disaster",0],["plague",3],["drama",2],["comedy",1],["aftermath",6],["catastrophe",0],["misfortune",2],["horror",6],["calamity",0]],"en":"That autumn a flood turned the low town into a real tragedy. The disaster came at night, and in its aftermath whole streets stood under water. Some called it a catastrophe, a plain calamity, others simply bad fortune, but for the old theatre it was a heavy misfortune. A sickness, like a plague, followed the water and closed the schools for a week. The actors had planned a comedy that month, and now they changed it into a tragic play about the town. The drama would open with the sound of rain. Few could sit through it without a shiver of horror. Yet the little hall was full, and people clapped for a long time.","zh":"那年秋天，一场洪水把低处的镇子变成了真正的悲剧。灾难在夜里降临，灾后的情景是整条整条街泡在水里。有人叫它大灾，有人只说是倒霉，可对那座老剧院来说，这是一场沉重的厄运。疫病像瘟疫一样跟着水来了，让学校停课一周。演员们本打算那个月演一出喜剧，如今把它改成了一出关于这座镇的悲剧。这出戏会以雨声开场。很少有人能坐着看完而不打一个寒颤。可小礼堂还是坐满了人，掌声响了很久。"},"trail":{"tw":[["trailer",4],["dog",0],["tree",3],["travel",2],["road",6],["lead",0],["slot",3],["drag",2],["creek",6],["tail",0]],"en":"Early one morning my dog and I set out to follow a narrow trail through the hills. We had travelled this road before, but the winter rain had changed it. A fallen tree blocked one bend, and I had to drag a branch out of the way. My dog would lead me across a shallow creek and then wait, tail high. Near noon we reached a slot between two rocks, so narrow that we had to go one at a time. Behind us came a small trailer, pulled by a farmer who knew the way. The path was long, and our legs were tired. Still, the quiet at the top was worth every step.","zh":"一天清早，我和我的狗出发，顺着一条窄窄的小径穿过山丘。这条路我们以前走过，可冬天的雨把它变得不一样了。一棵倒下的树挡住了拐弯处，我只好把一根树枝拖开。我的狗会领我蹚过一条浅浅的小溪，然后高高翘着尾巴等我。快中午时，我们走到两块岩石之间的一个窄缝，窄得只能一个一个地过去。我们身后跟来一辆小拖车，由一个认路的农夫拉着。路很长，我们的腿都累了。可山顶上的那份安静，值每一步。"},"tube":{"tw":[["tubular",4],["pipe",3],["drain",3],["bring",2],["valve",6],["subway",0],["vessel",3],["ride",2],["fuse",6],["metro",0]],"en":"Last month the drain under our street began to leak into a long tube. A plumber arrived with a metal pipe and a new valve, and he had to bring a heavy bag of tools down the narrow stairs. The old part was tubular and thin, so water would rush through it like a small stream. He closed the valve first, then took the whole section apart. A blocked fuse in the pump is often the real cause, he said. That evening I had to ride the subway, then the metro, to the far edge of town for a spare part. A small vessel of hot water waited for me at home. By midnight the pipe was dry, and the street was quiet again.","zh":"上个月，我们街下的排水道开始往一根长管子里漏水。一个水暖工带着一截金属管和一个新阀门来了，还得把一大包工具搬下窄窄的楼梯。旧的那段是管状的，又薄，水像小溪一样冲过去。他先关掉阀门，再把整段拆开。他说，水泵里烧断的保险丝常常才是真正的病根。那天傍晚，我不得不先坐地铁再换通勤线，去城的另一头买配件。家里有一小壶热水等着我。到半夜，管子干了，街上又安静下来。"},"urge":{"tw":[["urgent",4],["press",0],["push",3],["desire",2],["persuade",6],["cheer",0],["rush",3],["encourage",2],["invite",6],["recommend",0]],"en":"At the last race of the season the coach felt an urgent need to urge his runner on. He would press the young man's shoulder and push him toward the starting line. The runner had a strong desire to win, yet his legs were shaking. The coach tried to persuade him that fear was normal, and that the crowd was there to cheer. He said there was no need to rush and told him to run his own race. Friends came to encourage him from the fence, and someone would invite the whole family to watch. He finished third, and the coach would recommend him for the next level. That evening the boy smiled for the first time in weeks.","zh":"赛季最后一场比赛上，教练感到一种迫切的冲动，非要推着他的选手往前。他会按着年轻人的肩膀，把他往起跑线那边推。选手一心想赢，可两条腿在发抖。教练想让他相信，害怕是正常的，看台上的人是来给他加油的。他说不用急，跑好自己的就行。朋友们趴在栏杆边给他鼓劲，还有人要把全家都请来看。他跑了第三，教练打算推荐他进下一级别。那天晚上，这孩子几个星期来头一次笑了。"},"volume":{"tw":[["voluminous",4],["book",0],["capacity",3],["measure",2],["value",6],["mass",0],["novel",3],["magnitude",2],["output",6],["bulk",0]],"en":"The small press decided to publish a long novel in three separate volumes. The writer's notes were so voluminous that the editor had to measure them by weight. Each book had a different cover, and the first volume sold out in a week. The capacity of the old print room was low, so the output stayed small. The owner wondered about the value of a thick mass of paper in a digital age. Still, the bulk of the orders came from small shops in the countryside. No one could guess the magnitude of the writer's fame. By winter the second volume was already on the shelves.","zh":"这家小出版社决定把一部很长的小说分三卷出版。作者的笔记多得吓人，编辑只好按重量去衡量。每本书封面都不同，第一卷一周就卖光。老印刷间的能力有限，产量也就一直不大。老板琢磨着，在这个数字时代，一大摞纸还有什么价值。不过，订单里的大部分还是来自乡间的小书店。谁也猜不出这位作家的名气有多大。到冬天，第二卷已经摆上了书架。"},"render":{"tw":[["rendition",4],["picture",0],["bed",3],["coat",2],["appropriate",6],["return",0],["date",3],["pass",2],["try",0]],"en":"Each summer the old painter would return to the harbour and render the boats in oil. His rendition of the morning light was famous in the small town. He would choose a wide canvas and cover it with a thin coat of grey before he began. In front he liked to place a bed of bright flowers, so the picture would hold the eye. He always wrote the date in one corner with a fine brush. The colors he used seemed appropriate for the pale sky, and he would try new ones on a small board first. People would pass his easel and stop to watch. He never sold that painting; it hung at home until the end.","zh":"每年夏天，那位老画家都会回到港口，用油彩把那些船画下来。他画晨光的手法在这座小镇上很有名。动笔前，他总挑一块宽画布，先薄薄涂一层灰。前景里，他爱放一畦鲜艳的花，好让画面能抓住人的眼睛。他总用细笔在角落写上日期。他用的那些颜色跟灰白的天空很相称，新颜色他会先在小木板上试一试。路过画架的人都会停下来看看。那幅画他始终没卖，一直挂在家里，直到最后。"},"reproduce":{"tw":[["reproductive",4],["multiply",0],["breed",3],["produce",2],["replicate",6],["procreate",0],["print",3],["repeat",2],["migrate",6]],"en":"Every spring the birds return to the marsh to reproduce. This place offers them everything they need for their reproductive season: quiet water, tall reeds, and plenty of food. A pair will breed on the same nest year after year, and the numbers can multiply quickly. The female may produce eight eggs, though not all will hatch. A scientist came to replicate an old study and to print her results in a small journal. She would repeat her walk each week, counting the young. Many of these birds procreate only here, then migrate south when the cold comes. Some people say the marsh must be kept quiet for that reason.","zh":"每年春天，这些鸟都会回到这片沼泽来繁殖。这地方给了它们繁殖季所需的一切：安静的水面、高高的芦苇，还有充足的食物。一对鸟年复一年在同一个窝里生养，数量很快就能翻上去。雌鸟可能产下八枚蛋，不过并非都能孵出。一位科学家赶来重做一项旧研究，把结果印在一本小期刊上。她每周都要重走一遍同样的路线，数幼鸟。许多这样的鸟只在这里生殖，天一冷就往南迁。有人说，正因为如此，这片沼泽才必须保持安静。"},"sample":{"tw":[["sampler",4],["taste",0],["core",3],["example",2],["random",6],["try",0],["specimen",3],["consume",2],["data",6]],"en":"In the test kitchen a chef would take a small sample of every new drink. A young taster had first to taste each one and to try the sweetest. They would choose a core group of five people and ask them to consume the rest. Nobody was picked at random; each was an example of a different kind of customer. A thin glass tube held the specimen, and a machine would read the data. A music sampler in the corner played a soft tune while they worked. The head chef wrote down every answer on a long card. By noon the table was covered with empty cups.","zh":"在试味厨房里，厨师会给每一种新饮料取一小份样品。一个年轻试味员得先尝每一杯，再挑出最甜的那款。他们会挑出五个核心成员，让其余的人喝掉剩下的。人不是随便挑的；每个人代表一类不同的顾客。一根细玻璃管里装着标本，一台机器来读数据。角上一台音乐采样器一边放着轻音乐，他们一边干活。主厨把每个答案都记在一张长卡片上。到中午，桌上摆满了空杯子。"},"seize":{"tw":[["seizure",4],["assume",2],["carry",3],["hook",2],["smuggle",6],["attach",0],["catch",3],["confiscate",6],["grab",3]],"en":"At the port, officers had to seize a box of goods that someone tried to smuggle in. They would attach a small tag to each item before the seizure was recorded. One officer had to assume that the owner would not come forward, so the case moved fast. A metal hook was used to open the crate, and inside they found old coins packed in cloth. The law let them confiscate everything that had no papers. A young officer would carry the box to the office, holding it with both hands. He tried to grab a coin that slipped out, and the others laughed. Later they would catch the man at the gate.","zh":"在港口，工作人员必须扣下一箱有人试图偷运进来的货物。在把查扣登记下来之前，他们要给每件东西贴一张小标签。一位工作人员只能假定货主不会出面，所以案子办得很快。他们用一根铁钩撬开木箱，里面是旧硬币，用布包着。法律允许他们没收一切没有证件的东西。一个年轻的工作人员双手抱着箱子送去办公室。他想抓住一枚滑出来的硬币，旁边的人都笑了。后来，他们在门口把那男人逮住了。"},"trend":{"tw":[["trendy",4],["course",0],["fashion",3],["taste",2],["decline",6],["cut",0],["direction",2],["rise",6],["style",0]],"en":"Every year the owner of the small shop would follow the latest fashion. It was not easy, because taste would change with the season and the direction of the market was hard to read. One summer a trendy color became popular, and sales began to rise. The next year the same style saw a slow decline, and the owner had to cut his prices. He would course through the old stock and sell what he could. A smart buyer had to guess the trend before anyone else. He kept a small book of notes on each season. In the end he learned that a shop must change with the town.","zh":"每年，这家小店的老板都会跟着最新的时尚走。这并不容易，因为品味会随季节变，市场的走向又难捉摸。有一年夏天，一种时新的颜色流行起来，生意开始往上涨。到了第二年，同样的款式慢慢衰落，老板只好降价。他会把旧货一批批过一遍，能卖多少卖多少。一个精明的买家总得比别人先猜出风向。他留着一本小册子，记着每一季的情况。到头来他明白了，店得跟着镇子一起变。"},"rear":{"tw":[["back",5],["tail",3],["look",2],["front",1],["wheel",6],["behind",0],["pitch",3],["position",2],["gear",6],["bottom",0]],"en":"On the first drive of the year my uncle taught me the parts of the old car. He told me to look at the rear wheel before I moved an inch. The front wheel and the back one must both be firm, and the gear must sit in the right position. From behind you can see how the bottom of the car rides the road. He said a small pitch in the frame would show if something was wrong. Never start the engine with your eyes on the tail of another car, he warned. So I looked, and I listened, and I learned.","zh":"那一年的头一次开车，我叔叔教我认那辆旧车上的部件。他叫我先看后轮，再动一步。前轮和后轮都得结实，挡位也得挂在正确的位置上。从后面看，能瞧出车底在路面上跑得怎么样。他说，车架哪怕有一点点前后颠动，都能看出不对。他警告说，看别人的车尾开车，绝不要发动引擎。于是我看了，听了，也学到了。"},"retreat":{"tw":[["retire",0],["nest",3],["travel",2],["advance",1],["quiet",6],["withdraw",2],["nook",3],["signal",2],["battle",6],["recede",0]],"en":"After a long battle a tired soldier had to retreat from the hill with the rest of his line. They would travel through the night and withdraw into a quiet valley. Their commander had given the signal early, and there was no time to advance again. Years later he would retire to a small house in a nook of the woods. He liked the still mornings there, when the mist receded from the fields. A bird would build its nest under his roof, and he let it stay. He never spoke of that night unless someone asked. Peace, he said, is the only good signal.","zh":"一场恶战之后，一个疲惫的士兵只好带着剩下的队列从山岗上撤退。他们连夜赶路，退进一个安静的山谷。指挥官很早就下了信号，再没有时间反攻了。多年以后，他退休搬到林子里一个僻静角落的小屋。他喜欢那里静静的清晨，雾气从田地上退去。有只鸟在他屋檐下筑了巢，他由着它住。除非有人问起，他从不谈那一夜。他说，安宁才是唯一值得发出的信号。"},"reverse":{"tw":[["blow",0],["tail",3],["change",2],["forward",1],["trigger",6],["lift",0],["correct",3],["rule",2],["push",6],["opposite",0]],"en":"My father had to reverse the car down the narrow lane. The wheel would not go forward, so he had to push it gently with his shoulder. A small blow on the bumper had changed the shape of the tail, and he wanted to correct that too. The rule is simple, he said, look before you move. He would trigger the lights and lift his hand to signal each turn. The opposite side of the road looked wider, but it was not. In the end we reached the main street, and he let out a long breath. Driving backward, he said, teaches you to think forward.","zh":"我父亲只好把车倒着开下那条窄巷。方向盘往前推不动，他只能用肩膀轻轻顶着推。车尾让保险杠上的一记小撞改变了形状，他也想把它修正好。他说，规矩很简单，动之前先看。他打开车灯，抬手示意每一次转弯。马路对面那一侧看着更宽，其实并没有。最后我们终于上了主街，他长长舒了口气。他说，倒着开车，反倒教会你往前想。"},"reward":{"tw":[["honour",0],["price",3],["act",2],["penalty",1],["incentive",6],["advantage",0],["toast",3],["offer",2],["receive",6],["reinforce",0]],"en":"At the end of the year the small firm gave a reward to its best worker. The prize was not money alone; it was also a sign of honour from the whole team. To receive it, a worker had to show one good act after another, never for the price alone. There was a penalty for those who left the job unfinished, but that rule was rarely used. The manager believed an incentive worked better than fear, and this helped every worker see the advantage of care. That evening they raised a toast to the young woman who had won. Her quiet smile seemed to reinforce the whole room. Everyone offered her a warm hand.","zh":"年底，这家小公司把一份奖励给了最能干的员工。奖品不只是一笔钱；它也是整个团队的一份敬意。要拿到它，一个人得做出一个又一个好的举动，绝不是为了钱。活儿没干完的会有处罚，不过那条规矩很少用上。经理相信激励比害怕管用，这也让每个工人都看到了用心的好处。那天晚上，大家向这位得奖的年轻女工举杯。她那安静的一笑，仿佛让满屋子的人都更齐心。每个人都伸手要跟她握一握。"},"source":{"tw":[["root",0],["home",3],["document",2],["sink",1],["according",6],["origin",3],["spring",3],["facility",2],["data",6],["generator",0]],"en":"High in the hills a small spring is the source of the whole river. From its root in the rock, clear water runs down and becomes the stream that feeds the town. According to an old document, the first settlers drank here and called it home. A scientist came to test how far the water would sink into the ground below. Her data showed that the origin of the flow was not one spring but three. The town built a simple facility to guard the water and a small generator to power the pumps. Without this source, the valley would be dry. Few people ever visit it, and that is good.","zh":"高高的山里，一泓小泉就是整条河的源头。水从岩石的根缝里涌出，清亮地淌下去，汇成供全镇用的溪流。按一份旧文书说，最早来的人就在这儿饮水，把这里叫作家园。一位科学家来测水会往地下渗多深。她的数据表明，这股水并非出自一处泉眼，而是三处。镇上修了一处简单的设施守住水源，还装了一台小发电机带动水泵。没有这个源头，山谷就会干涸。很少有人去那里，这也是好事。"},"withdraw":{"tw":[["draw",3],["brush",3],["tire",2],["deposit",1],["accept",6],["recall",0],["shed",3],["travel",2],["negotiate",6],["remove",2]],"en":"Last spring I had to withdraw money from my account for a long trip. I would travel north for a month and needed cash for small shops that accept no cards. At the counter the clerk, who was a little tired that morning, asked me to sign twice. I had to draw a small sum each week and deposit the rest in a bank along the way. Please remove your hat, she said, and a short brush of doubt crossed my face. She had to negotiate the fee with her manager before I could recall the exact amount. I shed my coat and waited. In the end the money was ready, and I left with a smile.","zh":"去年春天，为了出趟远门，我得从账户里取钱。我要往北走一个月，还得备些现金，好在那些不收卡的小店里用。柜台后的办事员那天早上有点累，让我签了两回名。我得每周取一小笔，把其余的存进沿途的银行。她说，请把帽子摘一下，我脸上掠过一丝疑惑。她还得跟经理商量手续费，我这才想起确切的数目。我脱掉外套等着。最后钱备好了，我笑着离开。"},"yield":{"tw":[["afford",0],["fall",3],["accept",2],["stand",1],["bond",6],["bear",0],["leave",3],["agree",2],["value",6],["issue",0]],"en":"The small farm could not afford new machines, so the family had to sell the old ones. That year the yield of grain began to fall, and the value of the land went down with it. They would bear the loss and agree to plant less the next spring, though it was a hard issue for every family. A neighbour offered a bond that would pay a little each season, and they chose to accept it. The manager said the farm could not stand another bad summer. So they learned to leave the heavy work to a young team. By autumn the harvest was small but safe. Slowly the debt began to shrink.","zh":"这个小农场买不起新机器，一家人只好把旧的卖掉。那一年粮食的产量开始下滑，地的价钱也跟着跌。他们只得认下这笔损失，说好来年春天少种一些，可对每家来说这都是个难办的问题。一位邻居给了他们一种每季能收一点利息的债券，他们决定接受。管事的人说，这个农场再也经不起一个糟糕的夏天。于是他们学着把重活交给一支年轻的队伍。到秋天，收成虽少却很稳妥。债也慢慢缩了下去。"},"succeed":{"tw":[["succession",4],["follow",0],["hit",3],["fail",1],["future",6],["win",0],["pass",3],["step",6]],"en":"When my aunt grew too old to run the shop, the question of who would succeed her became urgent. Her son was the natural choice in the succession, but he was not sure he could win the trust of every customer. A single bad step, he feared, would make the small business fail. He decided to follow his mother for a year and to learn each task before he took it on. She would hit a good month, then a slow one, and he watched it all. In the future he hoped to pass the shop on to his own child. That spring he finally took the keys. Start small, she told him.","zh":"我姑妈年纪太大，经营不了那家店时，由谁来接她的班就成了急事。按顺序，她儿子自然是人选，可他不确定能不能赢得每位顾客的信任。他担心，走错一步，这点小生意就会黄。他决定跟着母亲一年，把每件事学会了再接手。她有时赶上一个好月份，有时又冷清，他全看在眼里。将来他盼着把店传给自己的孩子。那年春天，他终于拿起了钥匙。她告诉他，从小处做起。"},"sustain":{"tw":[["sustenance",4],["hold",0],["back",3],["admit",2],["support",0],["carry",3],["continue",2],["maintain",0]],"en":"A small farm must sustain a family through every season, good and bad. Around this house, food is more than sustenance; it is the whole year's work. The heavy sacks would hold the grain, and a wooden cart could carry the harvest to town. The father had to admit that one field alone could not support them all. So the family would continue to grow a second crop and to maintain the old stone wall in the yard. Neighbours came to help, and no one would hold back. In the hard years they shared what little they had. That habit is what truly sustains them.","zh":"一个小农场得养活一家人度过每个季节，好年景坏年景都得撑住。在这栋房子周围，吃的不只是果腹的东西；它是一年到头的活计。沉甸甸的麻袋盛粮食，一辆木车能把收成运进城。做父亲的不得不承认，单靠一块地养不起他们全家。于是这家人继续种第二茬庄稼，还一直维护院子里那道老石墙。邻居们来帮忙，谁也不会袖手旁观。在艰难的年头，他们把仅有的一点分着吃。正是这个习惯，才真正把他们撑了下来。"},"sweat":{"tw":[["sweater",4],["fret",0],["pull",3],["towel",6],["stew",0],["trouble",3],["pillow",6],["perspire",0]],"en":"After an hour in the sun, sweat ran down my face and I had to pull off my heavy sweater. My friend would fret about the small trouble with the pump, but I told him not to worry. We took a towel and dried our hands before we touched the wires. A pot of stew was cooking on a small fire, and the smell made us forget the heat. That night I began to perspire again, and my head ached on the pillow. I drank water and stayed still under the blanket. By morning the fever was gone, and the work could go on. Hard days, my mother says, are best met with a full pot.","zh":"在太阳底下干了一个钟头，汗顺着我的脸往下淌，我只好把那件厚毛衣脱掉。我朋友为水泵那点小毛病发愁，我让他别担心。我们拿了条毛巾，把手擦干才去碰电线。火上炖着一锅菜，那香味让我们忘了热。那天夜里，我又开始出汗，脑袋搁在枕头上发疼。我喝了点水，裹着毯子一动不动。到早上，烧退了，活儿还能接着干。我娘说，苦日子，最配一锅满满的炖菜。"},"transition":{"tw":[["transit",4],["conversion",0],["jump",3],["change",2],["process",6],["leap",3],["switch",2],["shift",6]],"en":"When the old plant changed what it made, the transition took a whole year. The first step was a slow conversion of the machines, and the whole process had to be planned month by month. Workers feared a sudden jump in the number of lost jobs, but the shift was gentler than they expected. Each team would switch to a new task only after two weeks of training. A small bus ran in transit between the old hall and the new one all day. There were hard days, and one big leap in cost. Yet the change held. By the next spring the plant made something new.","zh":"老厂改产的时候，这次转变花了整整一年。头一步是慢慢把机器改装过来，整个流程得一个月一个月地排。工人们怕一下子丢掉一大批岗位，可实际的变动比他们想的要缓和。每个班组都要先培训两周，才转到新任务上。一辆小巴整天在老车间和新车间之间来回跑。也有难熬的日子，成本还猛涨过一回。可这次改变立住了。到第二年春天，厂子做出了新东西。"},"rally":{"tw":[["ride",0],["kid",3],["call",2],["protest",6],["exchange",0],["jeer",3],["collect",2],["ahead",6],["tease",0]],"en":"A small rally filled the square with music and flags last Saturday. People would collect coins for the old library and ride in slowly on bikes. A young kid held a hand-made sign high above his head. A few men began to jeer, but most only wanted to tease them kindly. There was no angry protest, only a warm call for help. Friends would exchange news and stories all afternoon. The speaker said the town had to look ahead, not back at old quarrels. By evening the boxes were full.","zh":"上周六，一场小集会带着音乐和旗帜填满了广场。人们为那座老图书馆募钱，还骑自行车赶来。一个小孩把一块手写的牌子举过头顶。有几个人开始起哄，可多数人只是想善意地打趣他们。这不是什么抗议，只是一声温暖的求助。朋友们会换着聊上一下午的见闻。演讲的人说，这座镇子得往前看，别往回瞧。到傍晚，箱子都装满了。"},"rank":{"tw":[["absolute",0],["last",3],["body",2],["position",6],["order",0],["quality",3],["force",2],["class",6],["rate",0]],"en":"In the final test the students were placed in order of rank. The quality of their work would set each one in a clear position. My cousin came last in the first class, which hurt her pride. The teacher said no rank was truly absolute in a young mind. She had to force herself to study one extra hour a day. The school had to rate every single paper the same way. In the end a whole body of marks decided the list. She climbed two full places by spring.","zh":"期末考里，学生们按名次排成一列。他们答卷的质量会给每个人定下一个清楚的位置。我堂妹在头一次分班时排在最后，伤了她的自尊。老师说，在一个年轻人身上，没有哪个名次是绝对的。她得逼自己每天多学一个钟头。学校得用同一套标准给每份卷子打分。最后，一大摞分数定下了名单。到春天，她往上升了两名。"},"refuge":{"tw":[["resort",0],["shadow",3],["aid",2],["land",6],["asylum",0],["harbor",3],["shelter",2],["protect",6],["sanctuary",0]],"en":"The little cafe by the road became a refuge from the heavy rain. Travellers would resort to it when no bus came. Its wide roof could shelter a whole family. In the shadow of the old wall they found calm, and for a few lost strangers it even became a kind of asylum. A small garden gave aid to tired children with warm tea. The owner called the place a sanctuary for any lost walker. A boat in the small harbor gave the scene a gentle look. She said it was the safest land she knew, and she would always protect it.","zh":"路边那家小咖啡馆成了躲避大雨的一处避难所。没车来的时候，旅人就会投奔这里。它宽大的屋檐能把一家人护住。老墙的阴影里，他们找到了安宁；对几个走失的陌生人来说，这里甚至有点像庇护所。一座小园子用热茶帮了疲惫的孩子。老板娘把这地方称作任何迷路行人的圣地。小港湾里的一只船给这景色添了几分柔和。她说，这是她所知道的最安全的土地，她会一直护着它。"},"relieve":{"tw":[["excuse",0],["forgive",3],["better",2],["alleviate",6],["free",2],["spare",3],["rid",2],["cope",6],["save",0]],"en":"The new medicine helped relieve the pain in my aunt's back. It could alleviate the worst ache within an hour. The doctor had to excuse her from heavy work for a week. She hoped the rest would make her feel better soon. It would free her from the need to sit all day and help her cope with the stairs. A kind neighbour gave her a spare chair for the garden. She wanted to be rid of the old worry. In the end a short walk each day seemed to save her mood, and she began to forgive her own weak days.","zh":"新药帮婶婶减轻了背上的疼痛。它能在一小时里缓解最厉害的酸胀。医生只得免掉她一周的重活。她盼着休息能让她早点好起来。这能把她从整天坐着里解脱出来，也帮她应付楼梯。一位好心的邻居给她园子里添了一把多余的椅子。她想摆脱那份老担心。到最后，每天散一小会儿步似乎救了她的心情，她也开始原谅自己那些虚弱的日子。"},"resolve":{"tw":[["answer",0],["cut",3],["agree",2],["solve",6],["decide",2],["judge",3],["end",2],["compromise",6],["settle",3]],"en":"The two families met to resolve the old quarrel about the shared path. Each side wanted to settle the problem in peace. My father helped them agree on a simple rule. He would cut the argument short and ask one clear answer. A neighbour asked the old judge to decide the matter. In the end they found a small compromise that ended the fight. It was not a perfect solve, but it worked. Both houses used the path again the next morning. The street was quiet, and everyone slept well.","zh":"两家人聚到一起，化解关于那条共用小路的争吵。双方都想平平安安地把问题解决掉。父亲帮他们就一条简单的规矩达成了一致。他会把争论截断，只求一个清楚的答案。一位邻居请老法官来断一断这件事。最后他们找到了一个小小的折中，把这场架了结了。这算不上一个完美的解法，却管用。第二天早上，两家又都走那条路了。街上静了下来，人人都睡了个好觉。"},"respond":{"tw":[["answer",3],["accept",3],["act",2],["response",6],["reply",0],["field",3],["state",2],["urge",6],["react",2]],"en":"When the dry season came, the young trees in our field began to show stress. My sister, who studies plants, said they respond to a lack of water within days. Their first response is to close their leaves, and they react to heat by slowing their growth. She would urge the farmer to act before noon, and he had to answer her quickly and reply with a plan for the pipes. He did not accept the first idea, but the state of the soil left him little choice. In the end he agreed to water twice a week. The field looked better within a month.","zh":"旱季来的时候，我们田里的那些小树开始显出吃力的样子。学植物的姐姐说，它们对缺水的反应就在几天之内。它们最初的反应是把叶子合上，遇到高温就放慢生长。她总会催那位农夫趁中午前动手，他则得拿一套铺管道的办法来回应她。第一个主意他没有接受，可土壤的状况让他没多少选择的余地。最后他答应一周浇两次水。不到一个月，那块地看上去好多了。"},"restore":{"tw":[["doctor",0],["fill",3],["better",2],["consolidate",6],["fix",0],["piece",3],["change",2],["preserve",6],["repair",0]],"en":"The old clock in the town hall had stopped, and the council asked a young repair worker to restore it. An old doctor who loved such things came to help, because he wanted to preserve every small piece of the first design. They had to fill the worn holes with new wood and fix the broken case. For two weeks the work was slow, but each change made the numbers read better. Then they had to consolidate the loose parts before anyone could move the hands. In the end the repair was complete, and the clock kept good time again. No one could tell where the new work began.","zh":"市政厅那口老钟停了，议会请了一位年轻的修理师傅把它修复。一位喜爱这类东西的老医生也来帮忙，因为大家都想留住原来设计里的每一个小部件。他们得用新木料把磨出的洞填好，再把裂开的钟壳给修上。头两个星期进展很慢，可每改一处，钟面上的数字就走得更好一些。之后还得把松动的地方加固起来，谁都不敢碰指针。最后修复完工，那口钟又重新走得准了。新补的地方，谁也看不出来。"},"review":{"tw":[["survey",0],["check",3],["remember",2],["report",6],["critique",0],["notice",3],["exercise",2],["commission",6],["refresh",0]],"en":"Before the term test, our teacher gave us a short review of the whole book. She asked us to check our notes and to remember the main names from each unit. We did a small exercise every evening, and she would notice who had done the work. One student wrote a sharp critique of the story, and the class had to read it aloud. A survey at the end showed that most of us felt more ready. The school commission even asked her to write a small report about the method. A quick break helped refresh our minds before the exam.","zh":"期末考试前，老师带我们把整本书做了一次简短的复习。她让我们检查笔记，记住每个单元里的主要人名。我们每晚做一道小练习，谁做了她都看得出来。有个学生写了一篇尖锐的评论，全班还得把它读出来。最后的调查显示，我们大多数人心里更有底了。学校委员会甚至请她把这种方法写成一份小报告。考试前歇一小会儿，也让脑子清醒了不少。"},"route":{"tw":[["road",0],["beat",3],["send",2],["north",6],["path",0],["drive",3],["divert",2],["rail",6],["itinerary",0]],"en":"The bus driver had to find a new route after the heavy snow. The main road to the north was closed, so he had to divert the whole trip. My uncle had a paper itinerary, and he would send a message to the office at every stop. We had to drive behind a slow cart on a narrow path for an hour. He said the rail line was a better choice, but the next train would not leave until dark. Someone had to beat the snow off the roof with a long stick. In the end we reached the small town just before night. The road sign was half buried, but he knew the way.","zh":"大雪之后，公交车司机只好另找一条路线。往北的主路封了，他只能把整趟行程改道。我叔叔带了一张纸上的行程表，每停一站都给办公室发个消息。我们跟着一辆慢车，在一条窄路上开了一个钟头。他说坐火车更好，可下一班车要天黑才开。有人拿根长棍把屋顶的雪敲掉。最后我们赶在天黑前到了那个小镇。路牌被埋了一半，可路他认得。"},"scatter":{"tw":[["dust",0],["break",3],["separate",2],["hurl",6],["spread",2],["spray",3],["circulate",2],["scrape",6],["disperse",0]],"en":"When the old shelf came down in the kitchen, a cloud of dust began to scatter across the floor. A bag of flour had broken open, and the white powder started to spread everywhere. My mother had to separate the wet and dry things before they could stick together. She would hurl the empty bag into the yard and spray the table with water. Bits of glass seemed to circulate around the room as we swept. We had to scrape the floor twice to remove the last grains. In the end the air began to clear and the dust disperse, and we sat down to a late supper.","zh":"厨房那个旧架子塌下来时，一阵灰尘开始在屋里四散。一袋面粉摔破了口，白色的粉不停地往外撒。我妈赶紧把干的和湿的分开，免得粘成一团。她把空袋子往院子里一扔，又往桌上喷了水。我们扫地的时候，碎玻璃好像还在屋里打转。地板擦了整整两遍，才把最后几粒清掉。到最后空气慢慢清亮，灰也散了，我们才坐下吃了一顿迟晚饭。"},"scheme":{"tw":[["system",0],["body",3],["plan",2],["tax",6],["outline",0],["network",3],["plot",2],["loan",6],["strategy",0]],"en":"The town council put forward a new scheme to plant trees along every street. Their plan was to build a small water system first and then join each garden into one green network. A clear outline of the costs was shown to the public. The money would come from a special tax and a low-interest loan from the bank. Some people feared it was only a plot by two rich families. Others said the strategy was sound and would help the whole body of citizens. I joined a meeting where we discussed the scheme late into the evening. Work was to start in spring.","zh":"镇议会提出了一个新方案，要在每条街上种树。他们的计划是先建一套小型的供水系统，再把各个园子连成一片绿网。费用清单也向公众列得清清楚楚。钱来自一项特别的税和银行的一笔低息贷款。有人担心这不过是两户有钱人家的算计。也有人说这个策略稳妥，能惠及全体市民。我参加了一场会，大家讨论这个方案一直谈到夜里。工程定在春天动工。"},"slice":{"tw":[["cut",2],["section",3],["hit",2],["pie",6],["piece",0],["fillet",3],["share",2],["bread",6],["fade",0]],"en":"My aunt runs a small bakery, and every morning she would cut a fresh loaf into a thin slice for the first customer. Each piece had to be the same size, or she would give the larger share away. She kept a warm pie in the window, and the smell would hit anyone who walked past. In the back room she would fillet a fish for the lunch menu. A faded sign on the wall showed a section of the old prices. People came from all over the town for a slice of her bread. By noon the shelves were empty, and she would rest.","zh":"我姑妈开着一家小面包房，每天早上她都会把新出炉的面包切下一薄片，给第一位顾客。每一块都得一样大，不然她就把大的那份白送出去。她把一只热腾腾的馅饼摆在橱窗里，香味会撞上每个路过的人。里屋她还给午饭的菜单片一块鱼。墙上褪色的招牌上写着老价目的一部分。镇上各处的人都来买她的一片面包。到中午货架就空了，她才歇一歇。"},"slope":{"tw":[["side",0],["climb",3],["position",2],["steep",6],["pitch",0],["fall",3],["lean",2],["curve",6],["incline",0]],"en":"On our walk in the hills, the path began to climb along a long slope. The side of the hill was so steep that we had to lean forward with every step. My brother lost his position near the top and nearly had a fall. A line of old trees followed the curve of the land, and their tops seemed to incline toward the valley. We stopped at a rock where the pitch was gentle and sat down to catch our breath. Below us a small river ran through the field. Going down was easier, and we reached the car before dark.","zh":"我们在山里走的时候，小路顺着一个长长的斜坡往上爬。山坡那么陡，每走一步我们都得往前探着身子。我弟弟在快到山顶时没站稳，差点摔了一跤。一排老树顺着地势的弯度长着，树梢好像都朝山谷那边倾。我们在坡度平缓的一块石头旁停下歇口气。脚下一条小河穿过田野。下山轻松多了，天没黑我们就回到了车边。"},"sponsor":{"tw":[["shop",0],["godfather",3],["support",2],["challenge",6],["frequent",0],["guarantor",3],["advocate",2],["brand",6],["patron",0]],"en":"Every spring our small town holds a long race, and this year a local shop agreed to be the main sponsor. The owner had been a frequent patron of the park for years, so he wanted to support the young runners. He signed as the guarantor for the prize money, which was a real challenge for a shop of that size. A well-known brand also sent caps and water. My godfather, who is an advocate of clean sport, walked the whole course with the last runner. At the finish, everyone cheered. The event raised enough money to fix the old track.","zh":"每年春天我们小镇都办一场长跑，今年本地一家商店答应做主要赞助方。老板多年来常去那座公园，所以愿意支持这些年轻跑者。他为奖金做了担保人，这对那么一家小店来说是个不小的难题。还有个有名的牌子送来帽子和水。我的教父主张干净的比赛，陪着最后一名跑者走完了全程。到终点时，大家都在欢呼。这场活动筹到的钱，够把旧跑道修好了。"},"squeeze":{"tw":[["force",0],["drive",3],["move",2],["cut",6],["press",2],["bleed",3],["push",2],["crunch",6],["stuff",0]],"en":"The day we moved, we had to squeeze a large sofa through a narrow door. My father used all his force to press it from behind while I pulled. He could not move it more than a few inches at a time. A sharp edge began to cut into the wall. A small cut on my hand started to bleed, and the old wood gave a loud crunch. I had to push from the other side and hope the frame would hold. There was so much stuff in the room that the boxes blocked the hall. Then we had to drive it across town in a small cart. In the end it went through, and no one was hurt.","zh":"搬家那天，我们得把一张大沙发硬塞过一道窄门。我爸在后面用尽全身力气往前压，我在前面拉。一次也只能挪动几英寸。一个尖角开始往墙上刮。我手上划了个小口子，血渗了出来，旧木头也发出一声闷响。我只好从另一边推，只盼着沙发架子别散。屋里东西太多，箱子把过道都堵住了。之后还得用小车子把它拉过整个镇子。最后总算抬进去了，谁也没伤着。"},"stain":{"tw":[["mark",0],["dip",3],["change",2],["rust",6],["spot",2],["marble",3],["mistake",2],["paint",6],["brand",0]],"en":"An old marble table stood in my aunt's shop, and a dark stain had been left on it for years. She wanted to change the look of the whole top, but she was afraid of making a mistake. A worker would dip a cloth in oil and try to remove each spot and mark. Near the iron legs a patch of rust had grown, and the brand of an old maker was still faintly there. In the end she decided not to paint over it. The stain, she said, gave the table its story. Customers still came to see it.","zh":"我姑妈店里摆着一张旧大理石桌，上面留着一块深色的污渍，已经好多年了。她想把整个桌面改成别的样子，又怕弄出什么差错。有位师傅会用布蘸上油，试着把每个斑点和印记都擦掉。铁桌腿附近生出一片锈，旧工匠留下的牌子还隐隐可见。最后她决定不刷漆盖住它。她说，这块污渍正是这张桌子的故事。顾客们至今还来看它。"},"stake":{"tw":[["back",0],["pot",3],["kill",2],["share",6],["bet",2],["right",3],["mark",2],["venture",6],["game",0]],"en":"At the village fair, four friends sat down to play an old card game. The stake was small, but pride was not. Each put a coin in the pot, and the winner would take a share of it. My uncle made a quiet bet and did not show his hand. He said he would back the young player, because he liked a bold venture. There was a mark on one card, a tiny stain that gave it away at once. The others said it was not fair, and the game turned tense. One man even said he would kill the whole evening in anger. My uncle paid the right amount and left.","zh":"村里的集市上，四个朋友坐下来玩一种老纸牌。赌注不大，可面子要紧。每人往彩头里放一枚硬币，赢的人分走一份。我叔叔押得很轻，也没亮牌。他说他要支持那个年轻玩家，因为他喜欢冒险的劲头。有一张牌上带着个记号，一点点污迹立刻露了馅。别人说不公平，牌局一下子紧张起来。有个人气得说要把整晚都搅黄。我叔叔付了该付的钱就走了。"},"stem":{"tw":[["base",0],["branch",3],["check",2],["prevent",6],["bow",0],["stock",3],["form",2],["spread",6],["root",0]],"en":"In the school garden, my teacher showed us how a plant grows from a single stem. The base near the root was thick, and each branch carried a few leaves. She asked us to check the soil and to prevent any weed from taking the light. We had to bow low to see how the colour began to spread along the green form. A small stock of young plants stood in a box by the wall. Later she cut one stem and told us the story of that plant. I still remember the shape of it.","zh":"在学校的花园里，老师给我们看一棵植物怎样从一根茎长起来。靠近根的那截基部很粗，每根枝条上都带着几片叶子。她让我们检查土壤，还要防着杂草抢光。我们得弯下腰，才看得到那颜色是怎样顺着绿色的形体铺开的。墙边一个箱子里站着一小批幼苗。后来她剪下一根茎，给我们讲了那棵植物的故事。它的样子我至今还记得。"},"substitute":{"tw":[["exchange",2],["cover",3],["change",2],["minute",6],["replace",0],["double",3],["equivalent",2],["goal",6],["reserve",0]],"en":"On the day of the match, our best player could not come, so the coach had to find a substitute. He asked me to cover her place on the field, and I had to change my plans at the last minute. It was not an easy exchange, because no one could replace her, and her speed was almost double mine. The coach said I was an equivalent choice in skill, and I did not believe him. I told him my only goal was not to let the team down. He kept a reserve player ready on the bench, just in case. I played the whole second half. We did not lose, and that was enough.","zh":"比赛那天，我们最好的球员来不了，教练只好找个替补。他让我顶她的位置上场，我最后一刻不得不改变计划。这次替换并不容易，因为没人能真正替下她，她的速度差不多是我的两倍。教练说我在技术上和她不相上下，我却不信。我告诉他，我唯一的目标就是别让队伍失望。他还留了一名替补在长椅上，以防万一。下半场我踢满了全场。我们没输，这就够了。"},"sum":{"tw":[["add",0],["figure",3],["count",2],["nominal",6],["centre",0],["stuff",3],["state",2],["value",6],["heart",0]],"en":"At the end of the month, my mother would add up every bill and write the sum in a small book. The figure had to be right to the last coin. She would count the money twice and stack it at the centre of the table. Some of the prices were only nominal, and she would not let that stuff fool her. The state of the shop depended on that one number. She said the real value of the work was not in the money, but at the heart of it there was always a family to feed. Then she closed the book and turned off the light.","zh":"每到月底，我妈都会把每张账单加起来，把总数写在一个小本子上。这个数字一分都不能错。她会把钱数两遍，再码在桌子正中间。有些价格只是象征性的，她可不吃这一套。小店的状况全看这一个数目。她说这份活儿真正的价值不在钱上，可它的核心，总归是一家人要吃饭。然后她合上本子，把灯关了。"},"superior":{"tw":[["master",0],["better",3],["lake",2],["inferior",1],["appellate",6],["victor",0],["god",3],["religious",2],["court",6]],"en":"In our office the superior always said that hard work was better than luck. She had once been a victor in a long dispute with a rival firm, and her old master had taught her well. But she was not religious, and she refused to behave as if some god were watching. When the company took the staff to a lake for a weekend, she sat with us and told the story of the case. An appellate court had once ruled against her, and a young clerk, whom she had thought inferior, saved the day with one small note. She said no one is truly superior to another. We all laughed, and the weekend was fine.","zh":"我们办公室里那位上司总说，苦干比运气强。她曾在一场和对手公司的长期纠纷中胜出，是她的老师傅把她教得好。可她并不信教，也不肯装得好像有个神在看着。公司带大家去湖边过周末，她坐在我们中间，讲起了那桩案子。有一回上诉法院判她败诉，是一个她曾看不上眼的年轻职员用一张小纸条救了场。她说，谁也并不真比谁高一头。我们都笑了，那个周末过得挺不错。"},"supplement":{"tw":[["accessory",0],["appendix",3],["add",2],["ration",6],["append",0],["annex",3],["matter",2],["diet",6],["affix",0]],"en":"My doctor told me to take a daily supplement, because my diet was missing a key mineral. She said I should add more green food to every meal and keep each ration small. The little bottle came with an accessory, a small spoon, and a short appendix of notes. I had to affix a label to the box and append the dates on the sheet. It was not a small matter, she said, since the body needs time to change. She also handed me an annex about sleep. I followed the plan for a month, and felt stronger. The last page said the supplement was enough.","zh":"医生让我每天吃一种补充剂，因为我的饮食里缺一种关键的矿物质。她说我每顿饭都要多加些绿色蔬菜，每份的量要少。那个小瓶还带一件配件——一把小勺，外加一份短短的说明附录。我得在盒子上贴好标签，再把日期补记在表格上。她说这可不是小事，身体要慢慢才调得过来。她还递给我一份关于睡眠的附件。我照这个办法做了一个月，感觉结实了些。最后一页写着，这种补充剂已经够了。"},"survey":{"tw":[["follow",0],["overlook",3],["look",2],["estimate",6],["sight",0],["poll",3],["examine",2],["report",6],["study",0]],"en":"A team came to survey the old river before the town built a new bridge. They would examine the water every morning and follow the fish along the bank. From the top of a hill one could overlook the whole valley, a fine sight in the early light. The study had to estimate how many families lived near the water. A poll of the farmers showed they wanted the bridge in a different place. The leader wrote a long report and made us look at every number. In the end the plan changed. I helped carry the boxes of samples.","zh":"在镇上建新桥之前，一队人来勘察那条老河。他们每天早上检测水质，顺着河岸跟踪鱼群。站在一座小山顶上，可以俯瞰整个山谷，清晨的景色很好看。这项研究得估计有多少户人家住在河边。对农民的调查显示，他们希望把桥挪个地方。领队写了一份很长的报告，逼着我们把每个数字都看一遍。最后方案改了。搬那些样品箱的时候，我帮了把手。"},"swell":{"tw":[["great",0],["belly",3],["act",2],["shrink",6],["neat",0],["bulge",3],["grow",2],["creep",6],["well",0]],"en":"When we left the dough by the warm stove, it began to swell within the hour. Its neat round shape would grow into a soft belly with a fine bulge on top. My aunt said we should act fast and not let it creep out of the pan. If the room turned cold, the dough would shrink and the bread would not rise well. Baking was a great art, she said, and every loaf told you something. She covered it and let it rest. By noon the whole kitchen smelled warm and wonderful.","zh":"我们把面团放在暖炉边，不到一个钟头它就开始发起来。它那圆滚滚的形状慢慢胀成软软的肚子，顶上鼓起一小块。姑妈说我们得赶紧动手，别让它从盘子里爬出来。要是屋里转凉，面团就会回缩，面包也发不好。她说烤面包是一门了不起的手艺，每一炉都会告诉你点什么。她把面团盖好，让它静置。到中午，整个厨房都香得不得了。"},"task":{"tw":[["job",0],["adventure",3],["work",2],["mission",6],["tax",0],["enterprise",3],["duty",2],["force",6],["project",0]],"en":"My first task at the new office was to plan a small project for the winter. The manager said the job was simple, but it felt like a real adventure to me. Every member of the team had a duty, and no one could do the work alone. We had to force ourselves to finish before the tax season began. Our little enterprise had only four people and a tiny budget. It was a mission, the manager said, not just another day at a desk. By Friday the plan was on his table. He read it and nodded.","zh":"我在新公司的第一项任务，是策划一个冬季的小项目。经理说这活儿不难，可对我来说却像一场真正的冒险。队里每个人都有自己的一份职责，谁也单干不了。我们得逼着自己赶在报税季之前做完。我们这家小公司只有四个人，预算也很少。经理说，这是一项使命，不只是又一天坐在桌前。到周五，方案放在了他桌上。他看完，点了点头。"},"toss":{"tw":[["pass",0],["waste",3],["shake",2],["spoon",6],["sky",0],["dump",3],["throw",2],["cook",6],["flip",0]],"en":"In the kitchen my uncle would toss the salad with a wooden spoon and a quick shake of his wrist. He said you must not waste a single leaf. He could flip a pancake high toward the sky and catch it again. Then he would throw the empty pan in the sink and pass me a plate. His cooking looked easy, but I always made a mess. Once I let a whole bowl dump onto the floor. He only laughed and said not to worry. We ate outside as the sun went down.","zh":"在厨房里，我叔叔总会拿一把木勺拌沙拉，手腕一抖一抖的。他说一片菜叶都不能浪费。他还能把煎饼高高抛向天花板再稳稳接住。然后他把空锅往水槽里一扔，递给我一只盘子。他做饭看着轻松，我却总是弄得一团糟。有一回我让一整碗东西全扣在了地上。他只是笑笑，说别放在心上。太阳落山时，我们在外面吃饭。"},"transport":{"tw":[["carry",3],["bear",3],["move",2],["supply",6],["send",0],["bring",3],["please",2],["rail",6],["ship",0]],"en":"The company had to move a heavy supply of grain to the coast before winter. Good transport was the whole problem: the old trucks could not carry that load, and the rail line was far from the farm. They decided to ship it by water and to send two workers with the boxes. Those men had to bear long nights on the road. One of them said it did not please him, but the pay was fair. He would bring his own food and sleep in the cabin. In the end the grain arrived dry and safe. The manager thanked them both.","zh":"入冬前，公司得把一大批粮食运到海边去。运输本身就成了最大的难题：旧卡车装不下那么重的货，铁路离农场又太远。他们决定走水路，再派两个工人随箱子一起走。那两个人得在路上熬过好几个长夜。其中一个说这活儿他不乐意干，可工钱还算公道。他打算自己带上吃的，睡在船舱里。最后粮食干干爽爽、平平安安地到了。经理把两个人都谢了一遍。"},"treasure":{"tw":[["appreciate",0],["fortune",3],["love",2],["precious",6],["value",0],["recognize",3],["see",2],["ghost",6],["prize",0]],"en":"In the top drawer my grandmother kept what she called her only treasure: a small silver box. She would say its value was not in money but in the memory it held. Every child in the family learned to appreciate it and to recognize the name carved inside. She loved the story behind it more than any fortune. To her it was precious, and she would not see it sold for any prize. Once she said the ghost of her own mother still watched over it. We listened and said nothing. Years later, the box came to my sister.","zh":"在抽屉最里面，奶奶收着她口中的唯一一件宝贝：一只小银盒。她总说它的价值不在钱，而在它装着的记忆。家里每个孩子都学会了珍惜它，也认得盒里刻着的那个名字。她爱它背后的故事，胜过任何一笔财富。对她来说它无比珍贵，出什么价她都不肯看着它被卖掉。有一次她说，她母亲的身影还守着这只盒子。我们听着，什么也没说。多年以后，盒子传到了我妹妹手里。"},"triumph":{"tw":[["victory",0],["fall",3],["cheer",2],["defeat",6],["prevail",0],["glory",3],["success",2],["title",6],["crow",0]],"en":"The final match of the season felt like a triumph for our small school. We had lost so many times that no one expected a victory. In the first half our best runner took a hard fall, and the crowd stopped its cheer. But we did not accept defeat, and slowly our team began to prevail. A black crow watched from the fence as if it too knew the glory of the day. When the last point came, we won the title at last. My teacher said success is sweeter after a hard year. We carried the cup home together.","zh":"赛季最后一场比赛，对我们这所小学校来说像一次凯旋。我们输了太多次，谁也没想到能赢。上半场我们最好的跑者重重摔了一跤，观众的欢呼也停了。可我们没有认输，队伍一点点占了上风。一只黑乌鸦停在围栏上看，好像它也懂得这一天的荣光。最后一分拿下时，我们终于夺了冠军。老师说，苦过一年，成功才更甜。我们一起把奖杯捧回了家。"},"weave":{"tw":[["wind",0],["check",3],["travel",2],["stitch",6],["wander",0],["shoot",3],["design",2],["sew",6],["tissue",0]],"en":"In the old workshop, my aunt would weave a long cloth on a wooden frame. The design was simple, but she had to check every line before she could go on. She would wind the thread around a stick and travel down the row with slow care. When she had to sew a torn part, she used a fine stitch and a thin tissue of paper under it. Sometimes she would let her mind wander to the fields outside. A young worker would shoot pictures of the cloth for a small shop. We watched for hours. That cloth, she said, carried her whole life in its weave.","zh":"在那间老作坊里，姑妈会在一个木架子上织一长匹布。花样很简单，可每一条线她都要查过才肯往下织。她会把线绕在一根小棍上，再慢慢顺着这一行往下走。要补一处破口时，她用细细的针脚，底下垫一层薄薄的纸。有时候她会由着心思飘到外面的田野去。一个年轻工人会给这匹布拍些照片，拿去一家小店用。我们一看就是好几个钟头。她说，这一匹布里织着她一辈子。"},"substance":{"tw":[["substantial",4],["stuff",3],["idea",2],["steroid",6],["material",3],["matter",2],["alcohol",6]],"en":"The doctor warned my cousin that a white substance in a small bottle is not always safe. Some of that stuff is a steroid, and taking it without care can do real harm. Alcohol, he said, is another matter that many people treat too lightly. The main idea is simple: a strong body is built from food and rest, not from a powder. A substantial change takes months, not days. He asked her to read the material he had printed and to come back in a week. She put the bottle in a drawer and did not open it again.","zh":"医生提醒我表妹，小瓶里的白色物质并不总是安全的。其中有些东西是类固醇，不加小心地吃下去真会伤身。他说，酒精也是许多人太轻视的一样东西。核心的道理很简单：结实的身体靠的是食物和休息，不是粉末。真正的改变要花上几个月，不是几天。他让她把他打印的材料看完，一个星期后再来。她把瓶子放进抽屉，再没打开过。"},"raid":{"tw":[["bust",0],["swoop",3],["assume",2],["ambush",6],["foray",0],["attack",2],["bomb",6],["maraud",3]],"en":"At dawn the officers planned a raid on a warehouse by the river. They would swoop in from two sides and bust the whole group at once. No one could assume the place was empty, and they feared an ambush, so they moved with care. A short foray down the side road led them to a back door. The owner had tried to hide goods taken in an earlier attack on a shop. Someone said a bomb had once been found in the same yard. A stray dog would maraud through the bins at night. By seven, the place was quiet.","zh":"天没亮，警员们就计划对河边的一座仓库来一次突袭。他们会从两侧包抄进去，一下把整伙人抓个正着。谁也不能认定那里没人，所以他们行动很小心。沿着侧路的一次短促突击，把他们带到了后门。仓库主人曾把早些时候从一家店铺劫来的货物藏起来。有人说，就在同一个院子里曾发现过一枚炸弹。一条野狗夜里总在垃圾桶间乱扒。到七点，那地方安静了。"},"regret":{"tw":[["sorrow",0],["fear",3],["feel",2],["remorse",6],["repent",0],["inform",2],["apology",6],["rue",0]],"en":"My sister still speaks about the day she missed her father's last call. She would feel a deep regret every time the phone rang at night. A quiet sorrow stayed with her for months, and fear of losing more time changed the way she lived. She often said she wished she could repent, though there was no one left to forgive her. The remorse came in small waves. At last she wrote a long letter of apology to her aunt and asked me to inform the rest of the family. She would rue that missed call forever, she said, but she refused to let it stop her.","zh":"我姐姐到现在还会说起她错过父亲最后一通电话的那天。夜里电话一响，她就感到深深的遗憾。那份淡淡的悲伤在她身上留了好几个月，害怕再失去时间，也改变了她的活法。她常说想悔过，可已经没有人能原谅她了。悔恨一阵一阵地涌上来。最后她给姑妈写了一封长长的道歉信，还让我把这事告诉家里其余的人。她说，她会为那通错过的电话后悔一辈子，但她不肯让它把自己拦住。"},"reject":{"tw":[["refuse",2],["bounce",3],["accept",1],["oppose",6],["resist",0],["object",3],["agree",6],["decline",0]],"en":"At the small factory, every part that failed the test became a reject and went into a grey box. The manager would refuse to ship them, because he could not accept a single weak piece. Some workers would oppose the rule and resist the extra work. One of them would object that the test was too strict, and the others did not agree with him. He could only bounce the idea around and watch it decline. A young inspector learned to sort the parts by hand, and she said the reject pile told her more about the machines than any report. By spring the grey box was almost empty.","zh":"在那家小厂里，每一个没通过检测的零件都成了次品，被扔进一只灰箱子。经理不肯把它们发出去，因为他一个都不敢收。有些工人反对这条规矩，也不愿意多干那些活。其中一个人会提出异议，说检测太严，别人都不同意他。他只能把这个念头翻来覆去地想，眼看着它慢慢衰落。一位年轻的检验员学会了用手把零件分开，她说那堆次品告诉她的东西，比任何报告都多。到了春天，那只灰箱子几乎空了。"},"remedy":{"tw":[["cure",0],["ointment",3],["treat",2],["provision",6],["repair",0],["correct",2],["enact",6],["amend",0]],"en":"My grandmother kept a small tin of ointment that she called her best remedy. She would treat a burn or a cough with it and claim it could cure almost anything. The provision was simple: use it early and use it often. When a child fell and cut a knee, she would clean the wound and correct the dressing with steady hands. If the old jar cracked, she would repair it with tape rather than buy a new one. Years later the town council decided to enact a rule about selling such home-made medicine, then had to amend it twice. Grandmother only smiled and said a good remedy needs no law.","zh":"我祖母存着一小罐药膏，她管它叫自己最好的药。烫伤也好、咳嗽也好，她都拿它来治，还说它几乎什么都能治好。用的门道很简单：趁早用，勤着用。孩子摔破了膝盖，她就洗干净伤口，稳稳地把敷料摆正。旧罐子要是裂了，她宁可用胶带补一补，也不肯换新的。多年以后，镇议会决定就卖这种自制药品立一条规矩，后来又不得不改了两次。祖母只是笑笑，说真正的好药不需要法律。"},"request":{"tw":[["petition",0],["call",3],["wonder",2],["permission",6],["charge",3],["quest",0],["message",2],["pending",6]],"en":"A student sent a short message to the school office with one clear request. She wanted permission to hold a small meeting in the main hall on Friday. Her petition had seven names under it, and a fee, a small charge, was written at the bottom. The clerk told her the answer was still pending. 'I wonder if they ever read it,' she said on the phone, and her call was passed from desk to desk. The whole quest for a room took two weeks. At last the office agreed, and her request was granted. She stood in the empty hall and planned the seats.","zh":"一名学生给学校办公室发了一条简短的消息，提出一个明确的请求。她想获准周五在大礼堂开一个小会。她的请愿书下面签了七个名字，最底下还写明了一笔小小的费用。办事员告诉她，答复还没有定。'我不知道他们到底看没看过，'她在电话里说，她的电话被一个桌子转到另一个桌子。为了一间屋子，这一趟追寻花了两周。最后办公室答应了，她的请求得到批准。她站在空荡荡的礼堂里，安排起座位来。"},"resign":{"tw":[["free",0],["fall",3],["accept",2],["cabinet",6],["quit",0],["retire",3],["leave",2],["release",0]],"en":"After twenty years the manager decided to resign. The fall in sales that year made the choice easier, and she could no longer accept the long hours. She told the staff she would quit at the end of the month and then retire to a small house near the sea. In her office stood a wooden cabinet full of old files; she emptied it slowly. On her last day she felt free at last. The board agreed to release her from her contract early and let her leave before the weekend. A young worker took her chair and said, 'She taught me everything.'","zh":"干了二十年之后，这位经理决定辞职。那年销售下滑，让这个选择变得更容易，她也再也受不了那么长的工时。她告诉员工，她会在月底辞职，然后退到海边的一所小房子去。她办公室里立着一只木柜，里面全是旧文件，她慢慢地把它腾空。最后一天，她终于觉得自由了。董事会同意提前解除她的合同，让她在周末前离开。一个年轻员工接了她的位子，说：'她把什么都教给我了。'"},"resort":{"tw":[["repair",0],["shadow",3],["travel",2],["island",6],["refuge",0],["use",2],["posh",6],["haunt",0]],"en":"Every summer our family would travel to a quiet resort on a small island. The place was not posh, but it had become our favourite haunt over the years. In the shadow of the cliffs stood an old hotel that needed constant repair. We would use the same room each year and watch the sea from its window. When a storm broke the roof, the owner turned the dining hall into a refuge for the whole village. 'A resort is not only for guests,' he said. That autumn he began to fix the broken walls, and we promised to come back.","zh":"每年夏天我们一家都会去一座小岛上一个安静的度假地去旅行。那地方不算豪华，可这些年下来已经成了我们最爱去的地方。悬崖的阴影里立着一家需要不停修补的老旅馆。我们每次都住同一个房间，从窗口望海。有一场风暴掀了屋顶，老板就把餐厅变成了全村人的避难所。他说，'度假地不光是给客人住的。'那年秋天他开始修那些破墙，我们答应还会再来。"},"restrain":{"tw":[["hold",3],["rule",3],["control",2],["rein",6],["limit",0],["discourage",2],["curtail",6],["confine",0]],"en":"A young rider learned to restrain her restless horse on the first cold morning. She had to hold the reins tight and keep her own fear under control. The trainer gave one rule: never pull harder than the animal needs. For weeks she would limit every ride to a short circle inside the fence. When the horse tried to run, she did not shout but would gently discourage it with her voice. The cold would curtail their practice and confine them to the stable for days. Slowly the mare learned to walk behind her. In spring the two of them crossed the open field without a single fight.","zh":"在一个寒冷的清晨，一位年轻骑手学着管住她那匹不安分的马。她得把缰绳握紧，还得压住自己的恐惧。教练只给了一条规矩：永远不要拉得比牲口需要的更用力。好几个星期，她都把每次骑乘限制在围栏里的小小一圈。马想跑的时候，她不喊，只用声音轻轻地劝住它。天冷会缩短她们练习的时间，把她们困在马厩里好几天。慢慢地，那匹母马学会了跟在她后面走。到了春天，她们一起穿过开阔的田野，一次都没有顶起来。"},"restrict":{"tw":[["limit",2],["rule",3],["control",2],["regulate",6],["qualify",0],["tie",3],["provision",6],["confine",0]],"en":"Because of the dry summer, the town had to restrict the use of water in every home. A new rule was passed to regulate the pipes and to control the hours when gardens could be watered. One provision said that only those who qualify as farmers could draw from the river. The council would limit each family to a fixed number of litres a day. People who washed cars were told to tie a note on the tap, so the inspector could see it. Anyone who broke the rule would be confined to a fine. By October the lake had risen. The manager of the water office said the hard months had taught everyone to be careful.","zh":"因为夏天干旱，镇上只好限制每户人家的用水。一条新规矩出台了，用来管理管道，也控制花园可以浇水的时段。其中有一条写明：只有够得上农民身份的人才能从河里取水。镇议会把每家的用水限制在每天固定的几升。洗车的人被告知要在水龙头上系一张字条，好让检查员看见。谁违反这条规矩，就只能挨一笔罚款。到了十月，湖水又涨起来了。水务主管说，这几个难熬的月份让每个人都学会了小心。"},"reveal":{"tw":[["break",0],["blow",3],["tell",2],["detail",6],["discover",0],["spring",3],["suggest",6],["expose",0]],"en":"A young reporter began to dig into an old factory by the river, hoping to reveal what had happened there. A worker who had been fired decided to tell her the whole story and could not hide a single detail. Together they would discover that the company had dumped waste for years. The first sign came in spring, when dead fish floated near the bank. Tests would suggest the water was far from safe. Her report was a heavy blow to the owners, and it would expose them in front of the whole town. Some neighbours feared the story would break the local economy, but she kept writing. The factory closed that winter.","zh":"一位年轻记者开始调查河边那家老厂，想把它那里发生过的事揭出来。一名被开除的工人决定把整件事都告诉她，一个细节也不肯瞒。他们一起查明，这家公司多年来一直在倾倒废料。最早的迹象出现在春天，河岸边漂起了死鱼。检测表明，水质远远谈不上安全。她的报道对厂主是一记重击，也会让他们在整座镇子面前曝光。有些邻居担心这篇报道会拖垮当地的生计，可她照样写下去。那年冬天，厂子关了。"},"revive":{"tw":[["repair",0],["boot",3],["boom",2],["flagging",6],["animate",0],["stimulate",2],["derail",6],["renovate",0]],"en":"The old workshop had been closed for years, but a new owner hoped to revive it. He spent the first month on repair work and on the machines that would not boot. The town was in the middle of a small building boom, so there was demand for good wood again. At first the flagging interest of buyers worried him, and one broken order nearly derailed the whole plan. A grant from the council helped stimulate fresh training for young workers. He decided to animate the dusty hall with light and colour, then renovate the front room into a small shop. By autumn the saws were running again.","zh":"那间老作坊关了好多年，可有位新东家想让它重新活过来。头一个月他都在修补，还收拾那些启动不起来的机器。镇上正赶上一阵小小的盖房热潮，好木料又有了需求。起初买家兴致不高，让他发愁，一张没做成的订单差点把整个计划拖垮。镇议会给的一笔补助帮着促成了年轻工人的新培训。他决定用灯光和色彩让积灰的车间重新有了生气，再把前屋翻新成一个小店。到了秋天，锯子又响了起来。"},"rival":{"tw":[["touch",0],["king",3],["compete",2],["bid",6],["competition",0],["champion",3],["ally",6],["equal",0]],"en":"Two bakeries on the same street had been rivals for a decade, yet they never lost touch with one another. Each wanted to be the king of the morning trade and would compete for every customer. Once a year they entered the same bread competition, and the winner took home a small cup. This year the champion came from the older shop, but only by a single point. Both owners put in a bid to rent the empty corner store at the same time. In the end they became allies and shared it as an equal pair. 'A rival keeps you sharp,' said the younger one.","zh":"同一条街上的两家面包店已经较劲了十年，可彼此从来没有断了联系。两家都想当早晨这门生意的王，为每个顾客争个不停。每年他们都参加同一场面包比赛，赢家能捧回一只小杯子。今年夺冠的是那家老店，可只多了一分。两家老板又同时出价，想租下街角那间空铺子。最后他们成了盟友，像一对平等的伙伴一样把它合用。'有个对手，你才会保持清醒，'年轻的那位说。"},"scan":{"tw":[["read",0],["glass",3],["move",2],["ultrasound",6],["rake",0],["picture",2],["sensor",6],["skim",0]],"en":"The doctor had to scan the patient's leg before the operation. She began to read the notes while a nurse prepared the machine, a small box with a glass screen. The patient could not move his foot, so the team used a soft frame to hold it still. An ultrasound wave, guided by a fine sensor, moved across the skin and built a slow picture of the bone. The doctor would rake her eyes over each line of the image and then skim the older records for a comparison. 'Nothing is broken,' she said at last. 'But I want one more scan tomorrow.'","zh":"手术之前，医生得给病人的腿做一次扫描。护士准备机器时，她先看起了病历，那台机器是个带玻璃屏的小盒子。病人的脚动不了，于是团队用一个软架子把它固定住。一束超声波由一枚精细的传感器引导着，扫过皮肤，慢慢拼出骨头的图像。医生会仔细地扫过图像上的每一行，再浏览一下更早的记录作比对。最后她说：'没有骨折。不过明天我想再扫一次。'"},"scope":{"tw":[["reach",0],["sweep",3],["environment",2],["context",6],["background",0],["contrast",3],["extent",2],["range",0]],"en":"Before the field trip, our teacher explained the scope of the survey. The reach of the study would be one small valley, and a single sweep of the hills could take a whole day. We had to record the environment of every pond, not only the water but the plants around it. The background of each site mattered as much as the numbers in the front. To see the contrast, the class would compare a wet year with a dry one, and to that extent the work grew larger than we had planned. Our range of tools was small. In the context of a school project, that was enough.","zh":"出发去野外之前，老师讲了这次调查的范围。研究的触角只伸向一个小山谷，光是把山丘扫一遍就要一整天。我们得记录每个水塘的环境，不光是水，还有周围生长的植物。每处地点的背景和写在最前面的数字一样重要。为了看出对比，全班要拿一个雨水多的年份和一个干旱的年份相比，这样一来，工作量就比我们原先打算的更大。我们的工具种类不多。放在学校项目的背景下，这已经够了。"},"sequence":{"tw":[["episode",0],["rain",3],["film",2],["exact",6],["succession",0],["run",3],["order",2],["element",6]],"en":"Our small team was shooting the last episode of a short film about a village. The director wanted the exact order of each scene, so we had to write the sequence on a board before we started. One element was easy to forget: the rain, which had to fall in the same shot twice. We would run the camera, stop, and begin again in a slow succession of takes. In the original plan the story opened at the end, but we changed it after a long talk. By the third night everyone knew the sequence by heart. The final cut was only nine minutes long, yet it felt complete.","zh":"我们这个小团队正在拍一部关于村庄的短片最后一集。导演要每个场景都有确切的顺序，所以我们开拍前先把次序写在了一块板子上。有一个元素很容易忘：那场雨，必须在同一个镜头里下两遍。我们会让摄影机转起来，停下，再在一个接一个的补拍里重来。原计划里故事从结尾讲起，可我们谈了很久之后把它改了。到第三个晚上，每个人都把顺序背下来了。成片只有九分钟，却让人觉得很完整。"},"shield":{"tw":[["screen",0],["plate",3],["hide",2],["seal",6],["shell",0],["protect",2],["arrow",6],["harbor",0]],"en":"In the museum an old shield hung behind a glass screen. Long ago it had been made to protect a soldier from an arrow, and a thick plate of metal lay inside it. After the battle someone had used it to hide a small cup, pressing it against the shell of the wall. The caretaker would seal the room each evening and lock the case. Once, a storm pushed the sea past the harbor wall and water reached the hall. For a week the staff had to shelter the whole collection in a dry room. The shield stayed safe, and the small cup inside it was found again.","zh":"博物馆里，一面古老的盾挂在玻璃屏风后面。很久以前，它被做出来是为了替士兵挡住箭，里面还垫着一层厚厚的金属板。战后有人拿它藏过一只小杯子，把它紧紧贴着墙壳。管理员每天傍晚都会把展厅封好，锁上展柜。有一次，一场风暴把海水推过了港口堤岸，水一直漫进大厅。整整一个星期，员工们只好把整批藏品转移到一间干燥的屋里。盾安然无恙，藏在里面的那只小杯子也重新被找到了。"},"specify":{"tw":[["fix",0],["design",3],["choose",2],["assign",6],["condition",0],["detail",3],["plan",2],["determine",0]],"en":"Before the work began, the engineer had to specify every part of the new bridge. She would fix the measurement of each beam and design the joints on paper first. Then she had to choose the best material and assign a task to every worker. One condition was firm: the work could not stop the river below. Each detail, down to the smallest bolt, was checked twice. Her plan was long, but it helped the team determine the true cost before a single stone was laid. 'If you specify it now,' she told them, 'you will not argue about it later.'","zh":"动工之前，工程师得把这座新桥的每个部分都写清楚。她先定下每根横梁的尺寸，再在纸上设计好接缝。接着她得挑出最好的材料，给每个工人分派任务。有一个条件很硬：施工不能截断下面的河水。每一个细节，细到最小的螺栓，都要查两遍。她的方案很长，但它让团队在砌下第一块石头之前就弄清了真实的花费。'现在把话说清楚，'她对他们说，'往后就不用为它吵了。'"},"spill":{"tw":[["fall",0],["seed",3],["move",2],["waste",6],["talk",0],["run",2],["leak",6],["release",0]],"en":"One windy night a tanker began to leak near the coast, and oil started to spill into the sea. The crew tried to move the ship, but the wind would not let them run to the open water. By morning a dark line of waste had reached the beach where we plant seed each spring. Nobody could talk about anything else in the village. The company had to release a short statement and later pay for the clean-up. Some birds would fall into the black water and could not fly again. A young diver said the sea might need ten years to heal.","zh":"一个刮风的夜里，一艘油轮在近岸处开始漏油，石油涌进了海里。船员想把船挪开，可风太大，没法驶向外海。到早上，一条黑黑的废油带已经漂到了岸边那片我们每年春天播种的海滩。村里人除了这件事什么也聊不下去。公司只好发了一份简短的声明，后来又为清理掏了钱。有些鸟掉进黑水里，再也飞不起来。一位年轻潜水员说，这片海也许要十年才能缓过来。"},"target":{"tw":[["mark",0],["address",3],["goal",2],["likely",6],["direct",0],["clout",3],["increase",6],["object",0]],"en":"The manager set a clear target for the little bookshop: to sell two hundred copies in a month. She would mark the number on the wall so everyone could see the goal. To reach it, the staff had to address the slow afternoon hours and find new ways to direct readers to the back room. They printed a small card with the address of the shop and handed it out in the market. Sales were likely to climb slowly, not jump. The owner used his clout with a local school to bring in a class for a reading day. The increase at the end of the month was small, but the object had been met.","zh":"经理给这家小书店定了一个明确的目标：一个月卖掉两百本。她把这个数字标在墙上，好让大家都能看见这个目标。要达到它，店员们得着手处理午后那段冷清的时段，还得想新办法把读者引到里屋去。他们印了一张写着书店地址的小卡片，拿到集市上去发。销量多半会慢慢往上爬，不会一下子跳起来。老板动用他在一所本地学校的关系，请来一个班参加阅读日。月底涨得不多，可目标是达到了。"},"translate":{"tw":[["read",0],["gloss",3],["change",2],["compare",6],["understand",2],["move",2],["derive",6],["interpret",0]],"en":"My cousin found an old letter in a wooden box and asked me to translate it. I had to read every line slowly, because the handwriting had changed its shape over the years. A few words had a gloss in the margin, but most had none. It was hard to understand why the writer mixed two languages in one page. To interpret the meaning, I would compare the letter with a diary from the same year and find where the two stories touched. The work moved slowly, one small step each night. In the end I could derive one clear fact: the writer had been far from home.","zh":"我表妹在一只木箱里找到一封旧信，让我把它翻译出来。我只好一行一行慢慢地读，因为字迹这些年来已经变了样。有几个词在页边有一行注释，大多数却没有。很难弄明白写信的人为什么在一页里混用两种语言。为了理解它的意思，我会把这封信和同年的一本日记放在一起比对，找出两段故事相接的地方。活儿进展得很慢，每晚只往前挪一小步。最后我能从中得出一个清楚的事实：写信的人当时离家很远。"},"transmit":{"tw":[["air",0],["bring",3],["move",2],["detect",6],["carry",0],["project",3],["signal",6],["send",3]],"en":"For three cold days the small radio team worked to transmit a clear signal from the top of the hill. The tower could carry sound through the air for many miles, but a storm had bent one of its arms. A helper had to move the heavy box up the slope on a cart. His job was to bring the spare parts and then send a test message to the base. A small screen was set up to detect any fault in the line. At night they would project the light of a lamp toward the valley so the others could follow. On the fourth morning the music came back clearly, and the village clapped.","zh":"连着三个寒冷的日子，这支小小的电台小队都在山顶忙着把清晰的信号发出去。铁塔能把声音通过空气送出好多里，可一场风暴把它的一只支架吹弯了。一名帮手只好用推车把那口重箱子往坡上挪。他的活儿是把备件运来，再给基地发一条测试消息。他们架起一块小屏幕，用来探测线路上的任何故障。夜里，他们会把一盏灯的光投向山谷，好让其他人跟上来。第四天早上，音乐又清清楚楚地响了起来，全村都拍起了手。"},"welfare":{"tw":[["benefit",0],["advantage",3],["good",2],["reform",6],["upbeat",0],["relief",3],["aid",2],["care",6]],"en":"Last winter the town began a small welfare program for families with no income. The aim was the good of the whole street, not the benefit of a few. One early advantage was that many children could finally join the school meal plan. A quiet reform followed: the office learned to give aid faster and with less paper. When the first payments arrived, an upbeat mood spread through the market. For a mother of three the money was a real relief. The program also paid for basic care of the sick and the old. By spring most people said it had worked.","zh":"去年冬天，镇上为一个没有收入的群体开了一项小小的福利计划。图的是整条街的好，而不是少数人的好处。很早显现的一个好处是，许多孩子终于能加入学校的午餐计划。接着有一次悄悄的改进：办公室学会更快地发放补助，用的纸也少了。第一批钱到账时，市场上弥漫着一股振奋的气氛。对一个带着三个孩子的母亲来说，这笔钱是真正的宽慰。计划还负担了病人和老人基本的照护。到了春天，大多数人都说这事办成了。"},"recruit":{"tw":[["enter",0],["engage",2],["hire",6],["raise",0],["enlist",2],["volunteer",6],["enrol",0]],"en":"The mountain rescue team needed to recruit two new members before winter. Anyone who wished to enter had to be strong and calm in bad weather. The leader would engage a doctor to check each newcomer's health first. They could not hire paid staff, so every helper had to volunteer. A young farmer decided to enlist after the first snow, and his sister chose to enrol with him. The team had to raise money for ropes and boots. By December the two new recruits knew every path on the hill. They were called out three times in the first month.","zh":"山地救援队需要在入冬前招募两名新成员。想加入的人都得身体结实，坏天气里也沉得住气。队长会先请一位医生来检查每个新人的身体。他们雇不起拿工钱的员工，所以每个帮手都得当志愿者。第一场雪过后，一个年轻农民决定报名加入，他的妹妹也选择和他一起注册入队。队伍还得为绳索和靴子筹钱。到十二月，两名新队员已经熟悉了山上的每条小路。头一个月里，他们就被叫出去了三次。"},"reform":{"tw":[["reclaim",0],["better",2],["plan",6],["regenerate",0],["change",2],["welfare",6],["rectify",0]],"en":"When the old market began to lose money, the town agreed on a plan for reform. The first step was to reclaim the empty stalls and change the way rent was set. A young manager promised to better the service and to regenerate the tired square with trees and light. The change would also improve the welfare of the workers who cleaned the place each night. If any sums were wrong, the office would rectify them within a day. Not everyone liked the reform, and some owners chose to leave. Two years later the market was busy again on every morning of the week.","zh":"那家老集市开始亏本以后，镇上同意了一个改革的方案。第一步是收回那些空着的摊位，并改掉租金定的办法。一位年轻经理承诺改进服务，还要用树木和灯光让疲惫的广场重新焕发生机。这次改动也会改善那些每晚打扫场地的工人的福利。账目要是出了错，办公室会在一天之内把它纠正过来。并不是人人都喜欢这场改革，有些摊主选择离开了。两年后，一周里每个早上，集市又重新热闹起来。"},"regulate":{"tw":[["govern",0],["dispose",3],["adjust",2],["deregulate",1],["prohibit",6],["order",0],["restrict",2]],"en":"The new office was set up to regulate the food market in the old district. Its job was to govern who could sell there, adjust the opening hours, and restrict the number of stalls on each street. The council also chose to prohibit the sale of meat that had no stamp. Some traders asked the office to deregulate the small stands and let them run freely. The staff had to order a full list of rules and then dispose of the ones that no longer worked. It took a year before the market was clean and calm. Prices, in the end, stayed about the same.","zh":"新设的这个办公室，是为了管理老城区那家食品市场。它的职责是管谁能在那儿摆摊、调整营业时间，还要限制每条街上摊位的数量。市政会还决定禁止出售没有盖章的肉。有些商贩请办公室放宽对小车摊的限制，让他们自由经营。工作人员得先理出一整份规条，再把已经行不通的那些剔除掉。过了一年，市场才变得干净又有序。到最后，价格基本没变。"},"resolution":{"tw":[["answer",0],["decision",2],["mandate",6],["result",0],["document",2],["treaty",6],["resolve",4]],"en":"On the first day of the year my sister wrote down one resolution in a small document. Her decision was to walk to work every morning, rain or shine. She said the answer to her tiredness was not more coffee but fresh air. For the first week the result was poor, and she nearly gave up twice. A friend helped her resolve never to miss a Monday. The old mandate of the family, she joked, was to start late and finish nothing. But this time she kept going, like a treaty she had signed with herself. By March the walk took only twenty minutes.","zh":"新年的头一天，我姐姐在一份小文件里写下了一个决心。她的决定是每天早上走路上班，风雨无阻。她说，治她疲倦的办法不是多喝咖啡，而是呼吸新鲜空气。头一个星期效果很差，她差点放弃了两回。一位朋友帮着她下定决心，绝不错过任何一个周一。她开玩笑说，家里传下来的老规矩就是开始得晚、什么也做不完。可这一回她坚持下来了，就像跟自己签了一份条约。到了三月，这段路只要走二十分钟。"},"resume":{"tw":[["survey",0],["abstract",3],["change",2],["begin",6],["sketch",0],["continue",2],["suspend",6]],"en":"After a long winter the workers were ready to resume the building of the new hall. The survey they had made in autumn still held, though one small change was needed in the roof. The manager kept a short abstract of the plan on his desk and a rough sketch on the wall. Work would begin again on the first warm Monday. The rain had forced them to suspend the digging for three weeks, and now they had to continue quickly. 'A break does not break the work,' he told the young crew. By June the frame stood tall and straight.","zh":"漫长的冬天过后，工人们准备重新开始修建那座新礼堂。他们秋天做过的勘查仍然有效，只是屋顶需要做一处小小的改动。经理桌上放着一份方案的简短摘要，墙上钉着一张粗略的草图。工程会在第一个暖和的周一重新开工。下雨逼得他们停了三个星期的挖掘，现在得赶快接着干。他对年轻的工人们说：'停一下，并不会把活儿弄断。'到了六月，框架已经高高地立着，笔直笔直的。"},"routine":{"tw":[["act",0],["rut",3],["software",2],["exercise",6],["bit",0],["conduct",6],["function",0]],"en":"Every morning my grandfather followed the same routine without a single word. He would act as if the clock were a friend, waking at five and walking to the yard. His little exercise was to lift a bucket of water ten times. After years the habit had become a rut, yet he loved it. He kept a small software program on an old phone to count his steps, one bit of help he did not need. The morning tea was a fixed function of the day, and its conduct never changed. 'A routine,' he said, 'saves you from thinking about small things.'","zh":"每天早上，我祖父都一声不响地照着同一套日常来做。他会把钟当成朋友，五点就醒，走到院子里去。他那点小小的锻炼就是把一桶水举十下。年复一年，这个习惯已经变成了一种刻板的老路，可他很喜欢。他在一部旧手机上装了个小程序来数步数，其实这一点帮忙他根本用不着。早茶是每天固定要做的一件事，做法从来没变过。他说：'有个固定的一套，就不用为小事费心思了。'"},"sanction":{"tw":[["approve",2],["back",3],["permission",2],["impose",6],["warrant",0],["confirm",3],["ban",6]],"en":"The board met to give a sanction to the new plan for the harbor path. With their approval the work could start in spring. They asked for permission from the town office first and would back the plan with their own money. One member wanted to impose a fine on anyone who left rubbish on the path. The chair said a written warrant had to confirm every penalty before it was used. Another member suggested a full ban on motorbikes in the quiet part. In the end they approved the path but delayed the fines. 'A sanction works best when everyone understands it,' said the chair.","zh":"董事会开会，为海港那条小道的新方案给出一份正式的核准。有了他们的同意，工程春天就能动工。他们先向镇上的部门申请了许可，还愿意自己出钱支持这个方案。有位成员想规定，谁在小道上丢垃圾就罚款。主席说，每一笔处罚都要有一份书面授权来确认，才能施行。另一位成员建议，在安静的那一段彻底禁行摩托车。最后他们批准了这条小道，却把罚款的事往后拖了。主席说：'一项制裁，得人人明白才最管用。'"},"sole":{"tw":[["lone",0],["bottom",2],["legitimate",6],["exclusive",0],["repair",2],["solitary",0]],"en":"The old man who repaired shoes worked in a lone shop at the bottom of the street. Behind the glass lay rows of tools he used for each repair, and a single shelf held the shoes of the whole town. One morning a woman brought in a pair with a hole in the sole. 'It is the only legitimate pair I own,' she said with a laugh. His work was quiet and almost solitary, yet he liked it. He could not give her an exclusive price, because the leather had to be ordered. He told her to come back on Friday. A day later the shoes looked new again.","zh":"那位修鞋的老人，在街尾一间孤零零的铺子里干活。玻璃后面摆着一排排他修鞋用的工具，还有一层架子放着全镇人送来的鞋。一天早上，一位妇人拿来一双鞋底破了个洞的鞋。'这是我唯一一双像样的鞋了，'她笑着说。他的活儿安静，几乎与世隔绝，可他就喜欢这样。他给不了她一个单独照顾的价钱，因为皮子还得去订。他让她周五再来。一天之后，那双鞋看上去又跟新的一样。"},"sovereign":{"tw":[["independent",0],["king",3],["assume",6],["supreme",0],["shah",3],["guarantee",6],["monarch",0]],"en":"In the history lesson we studied a small country that became a sovereign state after a long struggle. Before that, a king had ruled it as part of a larger land. The new leaders wanted to assume full power and to guarantee every citizen a voice. Some people said the monarch had been a kind ruler, and others called him the supreme cause of their trouble. A traveller told us about a shah in a distant desert land who lost his throne in a single year. The teacher asked us to think about what makes a nation truly independent. No one in the class could agree, and the bell rang before we finished.","zh":"历史课上，我们学到了一个小国，它经过漫长的斗争才成了一个独立自主的国家。在那之前，一位国王把它当作一片更大领土的一部分来统治。新的领导人想全面掌权，还要保证每个公民都有发言的机会。有人说那位君主是个好脾气的统治者，也有人说他正是他们这些麻烦的至高根源。一位旅行者给我们讲了一个遥远沙漠国度里的君王，他在一年之内就丢了王位。老师让我们想一想，究竟是什么让一个国家真正独立。班里谁也争不出个结果，铃响的时候我们还没讲完。"},"speculate":{"tw":[["suppose",3],["guess",3],["reason",2],["surmise",6],["reflect",0],["invest",2],["contemplate",0]],"en":"When the old corner shop closed, everyone began to speculate about what would come next. My neighbour would suppose it would become a coffee house, and another would guess it was a bank. We could only surmise, since no sign had gone up. I liked to reflect on the small things: the new paint, the plain windows. My father told us never to invest money in a shop we knew nothing about. One evening we sat on the step and would contemplate every possible owner. In the end it became a library, and no one had reason to complain.","zh":"街角那家老铺子一关门，大家就开始猜测接下来会是什么。我的邻居会猜想它要变成咖啡馆，另一个则猜是银行。因为一直没挂招牌，我们只能瞎揣摩。我喜欢琢磨那些小事：新刷的漆，光秃秃的窗户。父亲告诉我们，绝不能往一家自己一无所知的店铺里投钱。有天傍晚我们坐在台阶上，把每一个可能的东家都仔细想了一遍。最后它成了一家图书馆，谁也挑不出毛病来。"},"status":{"tw":[["position",0],["face",3],["state",2],["exception",6],["condition",0],["command",3],["term",6]],"en":"The inspector came to check the status of the old water tank. Its position on the hill made it easy to reach, but its condition was poor. The report said that in its present state it could hold no more than half. The manager had to face the fact that a repair could not wait for spring. In the short term they could only lower the level and hope for rain. As an exception, the council gave the work a high command of funds. A young clerk sent a short status message to every household that evening. Nobody had expected the news to travel so fast.","zh":"检查员来查看那座老水塔的状态。它立在山上，位置倒是好够着，可状况很差。报告说，以它目前的状况，只能装到一半。经理不得不面对这个事实：修它的事等不到春天了。短期内他们只能把水位降下来，指望下雨。作为特例，市政会为这项工程拨了一笔可观的资金。那天傍晚，一名年轻职员给每户人家发了一条简短的近况通知。谁也没想到消息会传得这么快。"},"summit":{"tw":[["top",0],["pinnacle",3],["reach",2],["meet",6],["breast",0],["visit",6],["crown",0]],"en":"Three friends set out before dawn to reach the summit of the old hill. The path was steep near the top, and the wind grew cold at the breast of the slope. One of them said the smallest peak in the range was the true pinnacle of the walk. They had agreed to meet at the stone marker and to visit the small hut below. From the crown of the hill they could see the whole valley and the river far away. It took five hours to climb and two to come down. At sunset they sat together, tired and quiet, and no one wanted to leave.","zh":"天还没亮，三个朋友就出发了，要登上那座老山的顶峰。靠近山顶的路很陡，到了山坡的当胸处，风也冷了起来。其中一个人说，这一带最小的那座峰，才是这趟路真正的顶点。他们早就说好在石标那儿会合，还要去看看下面的那间小屋。从山顶的高处望下去，整个山谷和远处的河都看得见。爬上去用了五个小时，下山用了两个。日落时他们一起坐着，又累又安静，谁也不想走。"},"tackle":{"tw":[["harness",0],["rise",3],["attach",2],["forward",6],["rig",0],["attack",2],["tight",6]],"en":"The workers had to tackle a heavy beam that no cart could carry. They used an old tackle, a set of ropes and wheels, hanging from a strong frame. First they had to attach the hook and pull the harness tight around the beam. The rise of the load had to be slow and even, so two men held the rope forward and back. If one let go, the whole rig could swing and attack the wall. Slowly the beam rose to the top of the frame. By noon it sat exactly where the plan had shown. 'Good rope, good hands,' said the foreman.","zh":"工人们得对付一根没有哪辆车拉得动的重梁。他们用了一套旧滑车，就是一组绳索和轮子，吊在一个结实的架子上。他们先得把钩子挂上去，再把绳套在梁上拉紧。重物升起的过程必须又慢又稳，于是两个人一前一后地把绳子稳住。只要有一个人松手，整套家伙就可能甩起来撞到墙上。那根梁慢慢地升到了架子顶上。到中午，它正好落在了方案标明的位置。工头说：'好绳子，好手劲。'"},"thrill":{"tw":[["charge",0],["fear",2],["pleasure",6],["kick",0],["stimulate",2],["delight",6],["bang",0]],"en":"My first ride on the big wheel gave me a thrill I still remember. There was a charge of fear in my chest as the seat climbed, and a strange pleasure too. The drop would stimulate every nerve, and just before it came I heard a loud bang from the engine. My sister sat beside me and could not stop laughing with delight. For her the whole thing was only a cheap kick, but for me it was something else. When we stepped off, my hands were shaking. 'You will want to go again,' she said, and she was right.","zh":"我头一回坐那个大转轮，那种激动劲儿我到现在还记得。座位往上爬的时候，我胸口一阵害怕，同时又莫名地快活。往下俯冲时每一根神经都被激起来，就在它到来前，我听见发动机里一声巨响。我妹妹坐在旁边，笑得停不下来，满是欢喜。对她来说这不过是图个便宜刺激，对我来说却不止如此。下来的时候，我的手还在抖。她说：'你肯定还想再来一次。'她说得没错。"},"trigger":{"tw":[["trip",0],["device",2],["reverse",6],["activate",0],["initiate",2],["sudden",6],["spark",0]],"en":"The engineer opened the small box and showed us the trigger inside. It was a simple device that could activate the fan in a second. Nothing would move, he said, until one small part began to initiate the turn. If you pushed it the wrong way, it could trip a second switch and reverse the whole cycle. A sudden change in heat was enough to spark the sensor. 'Every machine has one small thing it waits for,' he told the class. We each pressed it once, and the little fan started at every touch.","zh":"工程师打开小箱子，给我们看里面的触发器。那是个简单的装置，一秒钟就能让风扇启动。他说，除非有一个小零件开始带动转动，否则什么都不会动。要是推错了方向，它还可能触动第二个开关，让整个循环倒转过来。温度突然一变，就足以引发传感器。他对全班说：'每台机器都有一样小小的东西在等着。'我们每人按了一下，那台小风扇每次都转了起来。"},"troop":{"tw":[["flock",0],["crowd",2],["force",6],["parade",0],["march",2],["contingent",6],["promenade",0]],"en":"A troop of young scouts came through our village on a long march. Behind them walked a crowd of parents and a small contingent of older leaders. They had come as a force for the spring clean, and each one carried a bag for rubbish. At noon they held a short parade down the main street, then stopped for water. In the evening a slow promenade around the square let the youngest ones rest their legs. A flock of pigeons rose from the roof as they passed. By sunset the whole troop was gone, and the street was cleaner than it had been for years.","zh":"一队年轻的童子军长途拉练，从我们村里经过。跟在他们后面的是成群结队的家长，还有一小队年长的带队人。他们是为春季大扫除来的，每人手里都提着装垃圾的袋子。中午他们在主街上走了一趟短短的队列表演，然后停下来喝水。傍晚，他们绕着广场慢慢列队走了一圈，好让最小的那些孩子歇歇腿。他们经过时，屋顶上腾起一群鸽子。到日落时，整支队伍都走了，那条街比这些年任何时候都干净。"},"variety":{"tw":[["change",0],["breed",3],["category",2],["various",6],["mixture",0],["example",6],["motley",0]],"en":"The old market sold a wide variety of fruit in every season. Each breed of apple had its own row, and every category was written on a small card. The owner liked to give one free example to anyone who could not choose. His stall was a mixture of colour and smell, a motley wall of red, green and gold. When the weather change came, he would move the boxes inside in an hour. He sold various kinds of jam as well, made by his sister at home. 'People want choice,' he said, 'and I give them a little of everything.'","zh":"那家老市场每个季节都卖各种各样的水果。每一种苹果都有自己的一排，每个类别都写在一张小卡片上。摊主喜欢给挑不下来的人免费尝一个样品。他的摊子是一堆颜色和气味的混合，红、绿、金凑成一道花花绿绿的墙。天气一转，他一个小时就能把箱子都搬进屋里。他还卖好几种果酱，都是他妹妹在家做的。他说：'人们想要有得挑，我就每样都给一点。'"},"venture":{"tw":[["guess",0],["risk",3],["company",6],["adventure",0],["suspect",3],["subsidiary",6],["hazard",0]],"en":"My uncle put his savings into a new venture, a small delivery company of his own. He would guess the cost of each route and take a real risk on the winter months. It was an adventure he had wanted since he was young, and he did not suspect how hard the first year would be. A subsidiary of an older firm offered to share his vans for a fee. Ice on the roads was the biggest hazard, and one crash nearly ended everything. Still, by the second year he had three drivers and a waiting list. 'Every venture teaches you something,' he said.","zh":"我叔叔把积蓄投进了一桩新的冒险生意——一家属于他自己的小运输公司。他会自己估算每条路线的成本，冬天那几个月得冒真正的风险。这是他年轻时就想干的一场历险，而他没想到头一年会这么难。一家老公司下面的一间子公司提出出钱和他共用货车。路上的结冰是最大的危险，一次撞车差点把一切都断送了。可到了第二年，他手下有了三个司机，还有一长串等着接活的人。他说：'每一桩冒险都会教会你点什么。'"},"vision":{"tw":[["sight",0],["dream",3],["experience",2],["sense",6],["fancy",3],["sensation",2],["image",6]],"en":"My grandfather lost most of his vision in his last years. His sight had faded slowly, and a strange sensation would come and go in one eye. Still, he had a clear image of the garden he wanted, and he could hold it in his mind like a dream. In that sense he saw more than we did. His long experience told him where to put each seed without looking. Sometimes he would let his fancy draw a whole field of flowers on bare ground. 'A vision does not need eyes,' he said, 'only patience.'","zh":"我祖父在最后的那些年里，几乎失去了视力。他的目光慢慢黯淡下去，一只眼睛里时常会有一阵奇怪的感觉来来去去。可他心里对想要的那座园子却有一幅清楚的画面，像一场梦一样牢牢搁在脑子里。从这个意义上说，他比我们看得都多。凭着多年的经验，他不用看就知道每颗种子该落在哪儿。有时他任由自己的想象在空地上画出一整片花来。他说：'眼光不需要眼睛，只需要耐心。'"},"weigh":{"tw":[["consider",0],["measure",2],["exceed",6],["count",2],["quantify",2],["raise",6],["matter",0]],"en":"At the farm gate the old woman had to weigh every box before it left. She would measure the grain with a wooden scoop and then let the scale do the rest. If the load would exceed the limit of the small truck, she had to split it in two. Her helper liked to count the boxes aloud, one after another, all morning. It was not easy to quantify the loss when rain had spoiled a field, but she tried. She would raise the question at every meeting: does a low price really matter more than good food? Then she would consider each farmer's case, one by one, and mark the final weight on the paper.","zh":"在农场的大门口，那位老太太得把每一个箱子都过一遍秤，才让它出门。她会用木铲量谷物，剩下的交给秤。要是这车货会超过小卡车的载重，她就得把它分成两趟。她的帮手爱一整个上午把箱子一个个数出声来。雨水毁了一片地，损失有多大并不好量化，可她还是尽量去算。每次开会她都要提出这个问题：便宜的价格真比好的粮食更重要吗？然后她会把每个农户的情况一一考虑一遍，把最后的重量记在纸上。"},"zone":{"tw":[["district",0],["island",3],["region",2],["buffer",6],["partition",0],["separate",2],["border",6]],"en":"Our town set up a quiet zone near the hospital last year. The district council put a low buffer wall along the border of the area so that sound could not pass. A simple partition was built to separate the car park from the small garden behind. In the middle stood a little island of grass where nurses could sit at noon. Every region of the town was asked to draw its own plan for such a space. At first some drivers complained, but the change was easy to accept. By summer the zone was the calmest place in the whole district.","zh":"去年我们镇在医院附近划出了一片安静区。区里的委员会沿着这片区域的边界砌了一道矮矮的隔音墙，好让声音传不过去。他们又搭了一道简单的隔断，把停车场和后面的小花园分开。中间立着一小块草地，像座小岛，护士们中午可以在那儿坐坐。镇上每个片区都被要求为这样一块地方画一份自己的方案。起初有些司机抱怨，可这个改变很容易接受。到了夏天，这片区域成了整个区里最安静的地方。"}}});
